Output~2025-04-24 16:32:39.181943: [RequestOutput(request_id=26, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Describe the life and reign of King Charles II. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 61885, 279, 2324, 323, 31402, 315, 6342, 15274, 8105, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='King Charles II was the monarch of England, Scotland, and Ireland from 1660 to 1685. He was the eldest son of King Charles I and the second English monarch of the House of Stuart. Charles II was born on May 29, 1630, in St. James Palace, London, and was the third child of Charles I and his wife, Henrietta Maria of France.\n\nAfter the execution of his father in 1649, Charles II was forced into exile in France and the Netherlands, where he lived for the next 9 years. During this time, he was known as the "King of the Exiles" and was supported by the French court.\n\nIn 1659, Charles II returned to England and was restored to the throne following the Puritan Commonwealth, which had been established after the execution of his father. He was crowned on April 23, 1661, at Westminster Abbey.\n\nCharles II\'s reign is often referred to as the "Merry Monarch" due to his love of pleasure and entertainment. He was known for his lavish spending and his love of parties, theater, and music. He also encouraged the arts and sciences, and his court became a center of intellectual and cultural activity.\n\nDuring his reign, Charles II also worked to restore the Church of England and to re-establish the monarchy\'s authority. He was a strong supporter of the Church of England and worked to restore its power and influence. He also re-established the monarchy\'s authority by strengthening the power of the monarch and reducing the influence of Parliament.\n\nCharles II\'s personal life was marked by several scandals and controversies. He had numerous mistresses and illegitimate children, and his marriage to Catherine of Braganza, a Portuguese princess, was childless. He also had a close relationship with his mistress, Nell Gwyn, who was a popular actress and courtesan.\n\nDespite his personal scandals, Charles II was a popular monarch and was loved by his people. He died on February 6, 1685, at Whitehall Palace, London, after a long illness. He was succeeded by his brother, James II, who was the first Catholic monarch of England since the Reformation.\n\nOverall, Charles II\'s reign was marked by a combination of cultural and artistic achievements, as well as personal scandals and controversies. He was a complex and multifaceted figure who left a lasting impact on English history.', token_ids=[34655, 15274, 8105, 574, 279, 63854, 315, 9635, 11, 19627, 11, 323, 14990, 505, 220, 11247, 15, 311, 220, 8953, 20, 13, 1283, 574, 279, 74665, 4538, 315, 6342, 15274, 358, 323, 279, 2132, 6498, 63854, 315, 279, 4783, 315, 44632, 13, 15274, 8105, 574, 9405, 389, 3297, 220, 1682, 11, 220, 9892, 15, 11, 304, 800, 13, 7957, 31396, 11, 7295, 11, 323, 574, 279, 4948, 1716, 315, 15274, 358, 323, 813, 7555, 11, 74310, 27625, 23880, 315, 9822, 382, 6153, 279, 11572, 315, 813, 7126, 304, 220, 10513, 24, 11, 15274, 8105, 574, 9770, 1139, 61087, 304, 9822, 323, 279, 26746, 11, 1405, 568, 12439, 369, 279, 1828, 220, 24, 1667, 13, 12220, 420, 892, 11, 568, 574, 3967, 439, 279, 330, 34655, 315, 279, 1398, 3742, 1, 323, 574, 7396, 555, 279, 8753, 5590, 382, 644, 220, 10680, 24, 11, 15274, 8105, 6052, 311, 9635, 323, 574, 28101, 311, 279, 44721, 2768, 279, 14874, 13145, 38298, 11, 902, 1