d to arrange the animals within each group. For example, if we have (Chickens, Dogs, Cats), we need to arrange the 4 chickens, 2 dogs, and 5 cats within their respective groups.\n5. For the chickens, there are 4! = 24 ways to arrange them.\n6. For the dogs, there are 2! = 2 ways to arrange them.\n7. For the cats, there are 5! = 120 ways to arrange them.\n8. Since these arrangements are independent, we multiply the number of ways for each group: 24 × 2 × 120 = 5760.\n9. Finally, we multiply this result by the number of ways to arrange the 3 types of animals (6): 5760 × 6 = 34560.\n\nTherefore, there are 34560 ways to place the 11 animals in a row of 11 cages, such that all animals of each type are in adjacent cages.", token_ids=[32, 11670, 3575, 2268, 10267, 596, 1464, 433, 1523, 3094, 555, 3094, 1473, 16, 13, 1226, 617, 220, 19, 54623, 11, 220, 17, 12875, 11, 323, 220, 20, 19987, 11, 369, 264, 2860, 315, 220, 806, 10099, 627, 17, 13, 1226, 1390, 311, 31993, 1124, 304, 264, 2872, 315, 220, 806, 81947, 11, 1778, 430, 682, 10099, 315, 1855, 955, 527, 304, 24894, 81947, 627, 18, 13, 1226, 649, 1212, 555, 77218, 279, 220, 18, 4595, 315, 10099, 304, 904, 2015, 13, 2684, 527, 220, 18, 0, 284, 220, 21, 5627, 311, 656, 420, 512, 197, 9, 320, 1163, 875, 729, 11, 39525, 11, 51849, 340, 197, 9, 320, 1163, 875, 729, 11, 51849, 11, 39525, 340, 197, 9, 320, 35, 27403, 11, 63226, 729, 11, 51849, 340, 197, 9, 320, 35, 27403, 11, 51849, 11, 63226, 729, 340, 197, 9, 320, 34, 1900, 11, 63226, 729, 11, 39525, 340, 197, 9, 320, 34, 1900, 11, 39525, 11, 63226, 729, 340, 19, 13, 4800, 11, 369, 1855, 315, 1521, 28904, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 31993, 279, 10099, 2949, 1855, 1912, 13, 1789, 3187, 11, 422, 584, 617, 320, 1163, 875, 729, 11, 39525, 11, 51849, 705, 584, 1205, 311, 31993, 279, 220, 19, 54623, 11, 220, 17, 12875, 11, 323, 220, 20, 19987, 2949, 872, 20081, 5315, 627, 20, 13, 1789, 279, 54623, 11, 1070, 527, 220, 19, 0, 284, 220, 1187, 5627, 311, 31993, 1124, 627, 21, 13, 1789, 279, 1287