Output~2025-04-24 16:36:12.352728: [RequestOutput(request_id=149, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Compute the longest increasing subsequence of a given array? ### Input: arr = [7, 10, 8, 11, 9, 5] ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 23426, 279, 22807, 7859, 1207, 15880, 315, 264, 2728, 1358, 30, 17010, 5688, 25, 2961, 284, 510, 22, 11, 220, 605, 11, 220, 23, 11, 220, 806, 11, 220, 24, 11, 220, 20, 60, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="To compute the longest increasing subsequence (LIS) of the given array, we can use dynamic programming. Here's the step-by-step solution:\n\n1. Initialize an array `dp` of the same length as the input array `arr`, filled with 1's. This represents the length of the longest increasing subsequence ending at each position.\n2. Iterate through the array from left to right. For each element `arr[i]`, find the maximum value in the `dp` array that is smaller than `arr[i]`. This represents the length of the longest increasing subsequence ending at the previous position that is smaller than `arr[i]`.\n3. Update `dp[i]` to be the maximum of its current value and the length of the longest increasing subsequence ending at the previous position that is smaller than `arr[i]`, plus 1.\n4. The maximum value in the `dp` array represents the length of the longest increasing subsequence.\n\nHere's the Python code to implement this:\n\n```\ndef longest_increasing_subsequence(arr):\n    n = len(arr)\n    dp = [1] * n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j] and dp[i] < dp[j] + 1:\n                dp[i] = dp[j] + 1\n    return max(dp)\n\narr = [7, 10, 8, 11, 9, 5]\nprint(longest_increasing_subsequence(arr))  # Output: 4\n```\n\nIn this example, the longest increasing subsequence is `[5, 7, 8, 11]`, which has a length of 4.", token_ids=[1271, 12849, 279, 22807, 7859, 1207, 15880, 320, 43, 1669, 8, 315, 279, 2728, 1358, 11, 584, 649, 1005, 8915, 15840, 13, 5810, 596, 279, 3094, 14656, 30308, 6425, 1473, 16, 13, 9185, 459, 1358, 1595, 9996, 63, 315, 279, 1890, 3160, 439, 279, 1988, 1358, 1595, 1138, 7964, 10409, 449, 220, 16, 596, 13, 1115, 11105, 279, 3160, 315, 279, 22807, 7859, 1207, 15880, 13696, 520, 1855, 2361, 627, 17, 13, 55440, 1555, 279, 1358, 505, 2163, 311, 1314, 13, 1789, 1855, 2449, 1595, 1138, 1004, 60, 7964, 1505, 279, 7340, 907, 304, 279, 1595, 9996, 63, 1358, 430, 374, 9333, 1109, 1595, 1138, 1004, 60, 29687, 1115, 11105, 279, 3160, 315, 279, 22807, 7859, 1207, 15880, 13696, 520, 279, 3766, 2361, 430, 374, 9333, 1109, 1595, 1138, 1004, 60, 19154, 18, 13, 5666, 1595, 9996, 1004, 60, 63, 311, 387, 279, 7340, 315, 1202, 1510, 907, 323, 279, 3160, 315, 279, 22807, 7859, 1207, 15880, 13696, 520, 279, 3766, 2361, 430, 374, 9333, 1109, 1595, 1138, 1004, 60, 7964, 5636, 220, 16, 627, 19, 13, 578, 7340, 907, 304, 279, 1595, 9996, 63, 1358, 11105, 279, 3160, 315, 279, 22807, 7859, 1207, 15880, 382, 8586, 596, 279, 13325, 2082, 311, 4305, 420, 1473, 14196, 4077, 755, 22807, 1265, 76562, 5341, 15880, 11179, 997, 262, 308, 284, 2479, 11179, 340, 262, 11581, 284, 510, 16, 60, 353, 308, 198, 262, 369, 602, 304, 2134, 7, 16, 11, 308, 997, 286, 369, 503, 304, 2134, 1998, 997, 310, 422, 2961, 1004, 60, 871, 2961, 3894, 60, 323, 11581, 1004, 60, 366, 11581, 3894, 60, 489, 220, 16, 512, 394, 11581, 1004, 60, 284, 11581, 3894, 60, 489, 220, 16, 198, 262, 471, 1973, 35899, 696, 1138, 284, 510, 22, 11, 220, 605, 11, 220, 23, 11, 220, 806, 11, 220, 24, 11, 220, 20, 933, 1374, 12916, 478, 1265, 76562, 5341, 15880, 11179, 595, 220, 674, 9442, 25, 220, 19, 198, 14196, 19884, 644, 420, 3187, 11, 279, 22807, 7859, 1207, 15880, 374, 78744, 20, 11, 220, 22, 11, 220, 23, 11, 220, 806, 60, 7964, 902, 706, 264, 3160, 315, 220, 19, 13, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None)], finished=True, metrics=None, lora_request=None, num_cached_tokens=None, multi_modal_placeholders={})]
