. For each element, we check if it is already in the dictionary. If it is, we return that element as the first repeating element. If not, we add it to the dictionary. If we finish iterating through the array without finding a repeating element, we return `None`. \n\nWhen we run this code with the input `arr = [3, 6, 7, 1, 4, 6, 7]`, it returns `6`, which is the first repeating element in the array.', token_ids=[791, 3465, 374, 311, 1505, 279, 1176, 40916, 2449, 304, 279, 2728, 1358, 315, 26864, 13, 4815, 791, 1988, 1358, 374, 1595, 1138, 284, 510, 18, 11, 220, 21, 11, 220, 22, 11, 220, 16, 11, 220, 19, 11, 220, 21, 11, 220, 22, 60, 29687, 4815, 1271, 11886, 420, 3575, 11, 584, 649, 1005, 264, 11240, 311, 2567, 3839, 315, 279, 5540, 584, 617, 3970, 779, 3117, 13, 1226, 30729, 1555, 279, 1358, 11, 323, 369, 1855, 2449, 11, 584, 1817, 422, 433, 374, 2736, 304, 279, 11240, 13, 1442, 433, 374, 11, 584, 471, 430, 2449, 439, 279, 1176, 40916, 2449, 13, 1442, 539, 11, 584, 923, 433, 311, 279, 11240, 13, 4815, 8586, 374, 279, 13325, 2082, 311, 11886, 420, 3575, 1473, 14196, 4077, 755, 1176, 1311, 65977, 8053, 11179, 997, 262, 3970, 284, 5731, 262, 369, 1661, 304, 2961, 512, 286, 422, 1661, 304, 3970, 512, 310, 471, 1661, 198, 286, 3970, 24146, 60, 284, 3082, 198, 262, 471, 2290, 271, 1138, 284, 510, 18, 11, 220, 21, 11, 220, 22, 11, 220, 16, 11, 220, 19, 11, 220, 21, 11, 220, 22, 933, 1374, 18465, 1311, 65977, 8053, 11179, 595, 220, 674, 9442, 25, 220, 21, 198, 14196, 19884, 644, 420, 2082, 11, 584, 7124, 264, 734, 1595, 3983, 1311, 65977, 8053, 63, 430, 5097, 459, 1358, 439, 1988, 13, 1226, 9656, 459, 4384, 11240, 1595, 29412, 29687, 1226, 1243, 30729, 1555, 279, 1358, 13, 1789, 1855, 2449, 11, 584, 1817, 422, 433, 374, 2736, 304, 279, 11240, 13, 1442, 433, 374, 11, 584, 471, 430, 2449, 439, 279, 1176, 40916, 2449, 13, 1442, 539, 11, 584, 923, 433, 311, 279, 11240, 13, 1442, 584, 6381, 88335, 1555, 279, 1358, 2085, 9455, 264, 40916, 2449, 11, 584, 471, 1595, 4155, 29687, 48