Output~2025-04-24 16:38:04.628815: [RequestOutput(request_id=203, prompt='<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{"Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: What\'s the difference between a virus and a worm? ### Response:"}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n', prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 5018, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 3639, 596, 279, 6811, 1990, 264, 17188, 323, 264, 35311, 30, 17010, 6075, 3047, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='A common question in the world of computer security!\n\nA virus and a worm are both types of malware, but they differ in how they replicate and spread:\n\n**Virus:**\nA computer virus is a type of malware that attaches itself to a program or file on a computer. It replicates itself by copying its code into other programs or files, often causing harm to the infected system. A virus requires human interaction, such as opening an infected email attachment or running an infected program, to spread. Viruses can also be spread through infected software downloads, infected USB drives, or infected CDs/DVDs.\n\n**Worm:**\nA computer worm, on the other hand, is a standalone malware program that can replicate itself and spread from computer to computer without the need for human interaction. Worms can spread through vulnerabilities in operating systems, network vulnerabilities, or by exploiting weaknesses in applications. Once a worm infects a computer, it can spread to other computers on the same network or even across the internet.\n\nKey differences:\n\n* A virus requires human interaction to spread, while a worm can spread automatically.\n* A virus attaches itself to a program or file, while a worm is a standalone program.\n* A virus can cause harm to the infected system, while a worm can cause harm to the entire network or multiple systems.\n\nIn summary, while both viruses and worms are malicious software, they differ in their replication and spreading mechanisms. Viruses require human interaction to spread, while worms can spread automatically, making them more dangerous and difficult to contain.', token_ids=[32, 4279, 3488, 304, 279, 1917, 315, 6500, 4868, 2268, 32, 17188, 323, 264, 35311, 527, 2225, 4595, 315, 40831, 11, 719, 814, 1782, 304, 1268, 814, 46113, 323, 9041, 1473, 334, 53, 17402, 25, 1035, 32, 6500, 17188, 374, 264, 955, 315, 40831, 430, 85603, 5196, 311, 264, 2068, 477, 1052, 389, 264, 6500, 13, 1102, 29641, 988, 5196, 555, 32139, 1202, 2082, 1139, 1023, 7620, 477, 3626, 11, 3629, 14718, 11682, 311, 279, 29374, 1887, 13, 362, 17188, 7612, 3823, 16628, 11, 1778, 439, 8736, 459, 29374, 2613, 20581, 477, 4401, 459, 29374, 2068, 11, 311, 9041, 13, 9734, 4881, 649, 1101, 387, 9041, 1555, 29374, 3241, 31572, 11, 29374, 11602, 20722, 11, 477, 29374, 62437, 15302, 12757, 82, 382, 334, 54, 494, 25, 1035, 32, 6500, 35311, 11, 389, 279, 1023, 1450, 11, 374, 264, 44488, 40831, 2068, 430, 649, 46113, 5196, 323, 9041, 505, 6500, 311, 6500, 2085, 279, 1205, 369, 3823, 16628, 13, 74130, 82, 649, 9041, 1555, 52227, 304, 10565, 6067, 11, 4009, 52227, 11, 477, 555, 71701, 44667, 304, 8522, 13, 9843, 264, 35311, 34527, 82, 264, 6500, 11, 433, 649, 9041, 311, 1023, 19002, 389, 279, 1890, 4009, 477, 1524, 4028, 279, 7757, 382, 1622, 12062, 1473, 9, 362, 17188, 7612, 3823, 16628, 311, 9041, 11, 1418, 264, 35311, 649, 9041, 9651, 627, 9, 362, 17188, 85603, 5196, 311, 264, 2068, 477, 1052, 11, 1418, 264, 35311, 374, 264, 44488, 2068, 627, 9, 362, 17188, 649, 5353, 11682, 311, 279, 29374, 1887, 11, 1418, 264, 35311, 649, 5353, 11682, 311, 279, 4553, 4009, 477, 5361, 6067, 382, 644, 12399, 11, 1418, 2225, 42068, 323, 63000, 527, 39270, 3241, 11, 814