Output~2025-04-24 16:38:29.663934: [RequestOutput(request_id=215, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Describe the principle of the Law of Supply. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 61885, 279, 17966, 315, 279, 7658, 315, 30909, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='The Law of Supply is a fundamental concept in economics that describes the relationship between the price of a good or service and the quantity of it that producers are willing and able to supply. The principle states that, all other things being equal, as the price of a good or service increases, the quantity supplied of that good or service also increases. Conversely, as the price of a good or service decreases, the quantity supplied of that good or service also decreases.\n\nIn other words, the Law of Supply suggests that producers are more likely to supply more of a good or service when the price is higher, as they can earn higher profits. On the other hand, when the price is lower, producers are less likely to supply as much of the good or service, as they earn lower profits.\n\nThe Law of Supply is often depicted graphically as a supply curve, which shows the relationship between the price of a good or service and the quantity supplied. The supply curve is typically upward-sloping, meaning that as the price increases, the quantity supplied also increases. The supply curve is also typically assumed to be a positive relationship, meaning that as the price increases, the quantity supplied increases, and as the price decreases, the quantity supplied decreases.\n\nThe Law of Supply is an important concept in economics because it helps to explain how changes in price affect the quantity of goods and services that are produced and sold. It is also an important tool for businesses and policymakers to understand, as it can help them make informed decisions about production and pricing strategies.', token_ids=[791, 7658, 315, 30909, 374, 264, 16188, 7434, 304, 28989, 430, 16964, 279, 5133, 1990, 279, 3430, 315, 264, 1695, 477, 2532, 323, 279, 12472, 315, 433, 430, 24190, 527, 10032, 323, 3025, 311, 8312, 13, 578, 17966, 5415, 430, 11, 682, 1023, 2574, 1694, 6273, 11, 439, 279, 3430, 315, 264, 1695, 477, 2532, 12992, 11, 279, 12472, 17665, 315, 430, 1695, 477, 2532, 1101, 12992, 13, 82671, 11, 439, 279, 3430, 315, 264, 1695, 477, 2532, 43154, 11, 279, 12472, 17665, 315, 430, 1695, 477, 2532, 1101, 43154, 382, 644, 1023, 4339, 11, 279, 7658, 315, 30909, 13533, 430, 24190, 527, 810, 4461, 311, 8312, 810, 315, 264, 1695, 477, 2532, 994, 279, 3430, 374, 5190, 11, 439, 814, 649, 7380, 5190, 22613, 13, 1952, 279, 1023, 1450, 11, 994, 279, 3430, 374, 4827, 11, 24190, 527, 2753, 4461, 311, 8312, 439, 1790, 315, 279, 1695, 477, 2532, 11, 439, 814, 7380, 4827, 22613, 382, 791, 7658, 315, 30909, 374, 3629, 44894, 4876, 2740, 439, 264, 8312, 16029, 11, 902, 5039, 279, 5133, 1990, 279, 3430, 315, 264, 1695, 477, 2532, 323, 279, 12472, 17665, 13, 578, 8312, 16029, 374, 11383, 40872, 1355, 385, 10194, 11, 7438, 430, 439, 279, 3430, 12992, 11, 279, 12472, 17665, 1101, 12992, 13, 578, 8312, 16029, 374, 1101, 11383, 19655, 311, 387, 264, 6928, 5133, 11, 7438, 430, 439, 279, 3430, 12992, 11, 279, 12472, 17665, 12992, 11, 323, 439, 279, 3430, 43154, 11, 279, 12472, 17665, 43154, 382, 791, 7658, 315, 30909, 374, 459, 3062, 7434, 304, 28989, 1606, 433, 8779, 311, 10552, 1268, 4442, 304, 3430, 7958, 279, 12472, 315, 11822, 323, 3600, 430, 527, 9124, 323, 6216, 13, 1102, 374, 