Output~2025-04-24 16:41:55.846188: [RequestOutput(request_id=311, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Name 5 invasive species. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4076, 220, 20, 53354, 9606, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here are 5 invasive species:\n\n1. Zebra mussels (Dreissena polymorpha): Native to Europe, these small freshwater mussels have been introduced to North America and have caused significant ecological and economic damage.\n2. Kudzu (Pueraria montana var. lobata): Native to Asia, kudzu is a fast-growing vine that has spread rapidly across the southeastern United States, outcompeting native vegetation and causing significant damage to infrastructure.\n3. Lionfish (Pterois volitans): Native to the Indo-Pacific region, lionfish have been introduced to the Caribbean and Atlantic Ocean through the aquarium trade and have established themselves as an invasive species, preying on native fish and invertebrates.\n4. Emerald ash borer (Agrilus planipennis): Native to Asia, the emerald ash borer is a beetle that has been introduced to North America and has caused significant damage to ash tree populations, leading to widespread mortality and ecological disruption.\n5. Burmese python (Python bivittatus): Native to Southeast Asia, Burmese pythons have been introduced to the Everglades in Florida through the pet trade and have established a breeding population, preying on native wildlife and causing significant ecological disruption.', token_