Output~2025-04-24 16:43:05.739912: [RequestOutput(request_id=336, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Create a new recipe for flavorful noodles ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4324, 264, 502, 11363, 369, 94631, 61260, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='**Spicy Korean-Style Noodle Recipe: "Seoulful Stir-Fry"**\n\n Servings: 4-6\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n* 8 oz. rice noodles (or soba noodles)\n* 2 tablespoons Gochujang (Korean chili paste)\n* 2 tablespoons soy sauce\n* 2 tablespoons rice vinegar\n* 1 tablespoon honey\n* 1 teaspoon grated ginger\n* 1/4 teaspoon red pepper flakes (optional, for some heat)\n* 1/4 cup vegetable oil\n* 1 onion, thinly sliced\n* 2 cloves garlic, minced\n* 1 cup mixed vegetables (bell peppers, carrots, snap peas, mushrooms)\n* 1/2 cup cooked chicken breast, diced\n* 1/4 cup chopped green onions, for garnish\n* Sesame seeds and toasted sesame oil, for serving (optional)\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook the noodles according to package instructions. Drain and set aside.\n2. In a large skillet or wok, heat the vegetable oil over medium-high heat.\n3. Add the sliced onion and cook until translucent, about 3-4 minutes.\n4. Add the minced garlic and cook for an additional minute, until fragrant.\n5. Add the mixed vegetables and cook until they\'re tender-crisp, about 3-4 minutes.\n6. In a small bowl, whisk together the Gochujang, soy sauce, rice vinegar, honey, grated ginger, and red pepper flakes (if using).\n7. Pour the sauce into the skillet and stir to combine with the vegetables. Cook for 1-2 minutes, until the sauce has thickened slightly.\n8. Add the cooked noodles to the skillet and stir to combine with the sauce and vegetables.\n9. Add the diced chicken breast and stir-fry until heated through.\n10. Taste and adjust the seasoning as needed.\n11. Transfer the noodles to a serving dish and garnish with chopped green onions, sesame seeds, and a drizzle of toasted sesame oil (if using).\n12. Serve immediately and enjoy!\n\n**Tips and Variations:**\n\n* For an extra kick, add more red pepper flakes or use sriracha sauce.\n* Substitute chicken breast with tofu or tempeh for a vegetarian option.\n* Add some crunch by topping with toasted peanuts or chopped scallions.\n* Experiment with different vegetables, such as zucchini, bell peppers, or bok choy.\n\nThis recipe combines the bold flavors of Korean chili', token_ids=[334, 6540, 2912, 16526, 12, 2377, 452, 31707, 26371, 25, 330, 1542, 11206, 1285, 65292, 7424, 894, 1, 57277, 27318, 826, 25, 220, 19, 12, 21, 271, 334, 46847, 25, 57277, 9, 220, 23, 25616, 13, 20228, 61260, 320, 269, 11752, 64, 61260, 340, 9, 220, 17, 56588, 480, 5059, 9832, 526, 320, 42, 46295, 59717, 25982, 340, 9, 220, 17, 56588, 29839, 19737, 198, 9, 220, 17, 56588, 20228, 47205, 198, 9, 220, 16, 62611, 26828, 198, 9, 220, 16, 42384, 97276, 44768, 198, 9, 220, 16, 14, 19, 42384, 2579, 25349, 82723, 320, 13099, 11, 369, 1063, 8798, 340, 9, 220, 16, 14, 19, 10747, 36581, 5707, 198, 9, 220, 16, 38427, 11, 99531, 48715, 198, 9, 220, 17, 85388, 31735, 11, 94927, 198, 9, 220, 16, 10747, 9709, 24822, 320, 17696, 58573, 11, 62517, 11, 10885, 47136, 11, 48251, 340, 9, 220, 16, 14, 17, 10747, 30205, 16553, 17659, 11, 89964, 198, 9, 220, 16, 14, 19, 10747, 38525, 6307, 45697, 11, 369, 61016, 819, 198, 9, 64027, 373, 19595, 323, 93972, 92223, 5707, 11, 369, 13788, 320, 13099, 696, 334, 56391, 25, 57277, 16, 13, 12797, 279, 61260, 4184, 311, 6462, 11470, 13, 62368, 323, 743, 16038, 62