Output~2025-04-24 16:45:15.609503: [RequestOutput(request_id=386, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Describe the differences between a substantive and procedural law. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 61885, 279, 12062, 1990, 264, 67749, 323, 62781, 2383, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a response that completes the request:\n\nSubstantive law and procedural law are two fundamental concepts in the legal system that serve distinct purposes. Substantive law, also known as "law in the books," refers to the actual rules and regulations that govern the rights and duties of individuals and organizations. It is the law that defines the rights and obligations of individuals, businesses, and governments, and it is the foundation of the legal system. Substantive law is concerned with the what, why, and how of the law, and it is the law that is enforced by courts and other legal authorities.\n\nOn the other hand, procedural law, also known as "law in action," refers to the rules and procedures that govern the process of enforcing substantive law. Procedural law is concerned with the how of the law, and it outlines the steps that must be taken to enforce substantive law. Procedural law includes rules about how lawsuits are initiated, how evidence is presented, how trials are conducted, and how judgments are enforced. Procedural law is designed to ensure that substantive law is enforced fairly and efficiently, and it provides a framework for resolving disputes and enforcing legal rights.\n\nIn summary, substantive law defines the rights and obligations of individuals and organizations, while procedural law outlines the rules and procedures for enforcing those rights and obligations. While substantive law is concerned with the what, why, and how of the law, procedural law is concerned with the how of the law.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 2077, 430, 45695, 279, 1715, 1473, 3214, 4811, 535, 2383, 323, 62781, 2383, 527, 1403, 16188, 19476, 304, 279, 5897, 1887, 430, 8854, 12742, 10096, 13, 3804, 4811, 535, 2383, 11, 1101, 3967, 439, 330, 20510, 304, 279, 6603, 1359, 19813, 311, 279, 5150, 5718, 323, 14640, 430, 2633, 279, 3268, 323, 22006, 315, 7931, 323, 11351, 13, 1102, 374, 279, 2383, 430, 19170, 279, 3268, 323, 30255, 315, 7931, 11, 9873, 11, 323, 17047, 11, 323, 433, 374, 279, 16665, 315, 279, 5897, 1887, 13, 3804, 4811, 535, 2383, 374, 11920, 449, 279, 1148, 11, 3249, 11, 323, 1268, 315, 279, 2383, 11, 323, 433, 374, 279, 2383, 430, 374, 45421, 555, 19359, 323, 1023, 5897, 11527, 382, 1966, 279, 1023, 1450, 11, 62781, 2383, 11, 1101, 3967, 439, 330, 20510, 304, 1957, 1359, 19813, 311, 279, 5718, 323, 16346, 430, 2633, 279, 1920, 315, 62908, 67749, 2383, 13, 1322, 2041, 4269, 2383, 374, 11920, 449, 279, 1268, 315, 279, 2383, 11, 323, 433, 50729, 279, 7504, 430, 2011, 387, 4529, 311, 29262, 67749, 2383, 13, 1322, 2041, 4269, 2383, 5764, 5718, 922, 1268, 43986, 527, 33230, 11, 1268, 6029, 374, 10666, 11, 1268, 19622, 527, 13375, 11, 323, 1268, 59358, 527, 45421, 13, 1322, 2041, 4269, 2383, 374, 6319, 311, 6106, 430, 67749, 2383, 374, 45421, 14470, 323, 30820, 11, 323, 433, 5825, 264, 12914, 369, 53583, 42254, 323, 62908, 5897, 3268, 382, 644, 12399, 11, 67749, 2383, 19170, 279, 3268, 323, 30255, 315, 7931, 323, 11351, 11, 1418, 62781, 2383, 50729, 279, 5718, 323, 16346, 369, 62908, 1884, 3268, 323, 30255, 13, 6104, 67749, 2383, 374, 11920, 449, 279, 1148, 11, 3249, 11, 323, 1268, 315, 279, 2383, 11, 62781, 