Output~2025-04-24 16:46:20.344359: [RequestOutput(request_id=418, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Provide me a list of diseases that can be caused by smoking. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 40665, 757, 264, 1160, 315, 19338, 430, 649, 387, 9057, 555, 20149, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is a list of diseases that can be caused by smoking:\n\n1. **Lung Cancer**: Smoking is the leading cause of lung cancer and is responsible for about 80-90% of all lung cancer deaths.\n2. **Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD)**: Smoking damages the lungs and can cause COPD, a progressive lung disease that makes it difficult to breathe.\n3. **Heart Disease**: Smoking damages the cardiovascular system and increases the risk of heart disease, heart attacks, and strokes.\n4. **Emphysema**: Smoking can cause emphysema, a condition that damages the air sacs in the lungs and makes it difficult to breathe.\n5. **Chronic Bronchitis**: Smoking can cause chronic bronchitis, a condition that inflames and irritates the bronchial tubes and makes it difficult to breathe.\n6. **Pneumonia**: Smoking weakens the lungs and increases the risk of pneumonia, a serious infection that inflames the air sacs in the lungs.\n7. **Cancer of the Mouth, Throat, and Esophagus**: Smoking can cause cancer of the mouth, throat, and esophagus.\n8. **Cancer of the Bladder, Kidney, and Pancreas**: Smoking has been linked to an increased risk of cancer of the bladder, kidney, and pancreas.\n9. **Osteoporosis**: Smoking can increase the risk of osteoporosis, a condition that weakens the bones and increases the risk of fractures.\n10. **Premature Birth and Low Birth Weight**: Smoking during pregnancy can increase the risk of premature birth and low birth weight in babies.\n11. **Infertility and Impotence**: Smoking can reduce fertility in both men and women and increase the risk of impotence in men.\n12. **Gum Disease and Tooth Loss**: Smoking can cause gum disease and tooth loss by damaging the gums and supporting tissues around the teeth.\n13. **Eye Problems**: Smoking can increase the risk of cataracts, glaucoma, and age-related macular degeneration.\n14. **Weakened Immune System**: Smoking can weaken the immune system, making it harder for the body to fight off infections and diseases.\n15. **Rheumatoid Arthritis**: Smoking has been linked to an increased risk of rheumatoid arthritis, a condition that causes joint pain and swelling.\n\nIt's important to note that quitting smoking can greatly reduce the risk of developing these diseases and improve overall health.", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 1160, 315, 19338, 430, 649, 387, 9057, 555, 20149, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 43, 2234, 26211, 96618, 73699, 374, 279, 6522, 5353, 315, 21271, 9572, 323, 374, 8647, 369, 922, 220, 1490, 12, 1954, 4, 315, 682, 21271, 9572, 16779, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 1163, 8535, 4761, 1257, 535, 35962, 55892, 31974, 320, 34, 3143, 35, 33395, 25, 73699, 26186, 279, 45274, 323, 649, 5353, 68672, 35, 11, 264, 23053, 21271, 8624, 430, 3727, 433, 5107, 311, 37397, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 46484, 31974, 96618, 73699, 26186, 279, 41713, 1887, 323, 12992, 279, 5326, 315, 4851, 8624, 11, 4851, 8951, 11, 323, 53572, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 2321, 12989, 325, 1764, 96618, 73699, 649, 5353, 991, 12989, 325, 1764, 11, 264, 3044, 430, 26186, 279, 3805, 11347, 82, 304, 279, 45274, 323, 3727, 433, 5107, 311, 37397, 627, 20, 13, 3146, 1163, 8535, 20407, 331, 20000, 96618, 73699, 649, 5353, 21249, 31071,