Output~2025-04-24 16:46:54.947893: [RequestOutput(request_id=426, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Make a list of different types of cryptocurrencies. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 7557, 264, 1160, 315, 2204, 4595, 315, 45074, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a list of different types of cryptocurrencies:\n\n1. **Bitcoin (BTC)**: The first and most well-known cryptocurrency, created in 2009 by Satoshi Nakamoto.\n2. **Ethereum (ETH)**: A decentralized platform that enables the creation of smart contracts and decentralized applications (dApps), launched in 2015.\n3. **Litecoin (LTC)**: A peer-to-peer cryptocurrency created in 2011 as a faster and cheaper alternative to Bitcoin.\n4. **Ripple (XRP)**: A real-time gross settlement system (RTGS) and currency exchange and remittance network, launched in 2012.\n5. **Bitcoin Cash (BCH)**: A fork of Bitcoin, created in 2017 to increase the block size and allow for faster transactions.\n6. **Cardano (ADA)**: A decentralized public blockchain and cryptocurrency project, launched in 2017 with a focus on sustainability and scalability.\n7. **Stellar (XLM)**: An open-source, decentralized blockchain network and cryptocurrency, launched in 2014 for cross-border payments and asset transfers.\n8. **EOS**: A decentralized operating system that supports the deployment of industrial-scale dApps, launched in 2018.\n9. **Monero (XMR)**: A privacy-focused cryptocurrency that uses advanced cryptography to protect user transactions, launched in 2014.\n10. **Dogecoin (DOGE)**: A decentralized digital currency created as a joke in 2013, but has since gained a large community and use cases.\n11. **Tether (USDT)**: A stablecoin pegged to the value of the US dollar, launched in 2014.\n12. **Binance Coin (BNB)**: The native cryptocurrency of the Binance exchange, launched in 2017.\n13. **Chainlink (LINK)**: A decentralized oracle network that provides real-world data to smart contracts, launched in 2017.\n14. **Tezos (XTZ)**: A decentralized blockchain platform that allows for on-chain governance and smart contracts, launched in 2018.\n15. **EOSIO (EOS)**: A decentralized operating system that supports the deployment of industrial-scale dApps, launched in 2018.\n\nThis is not an exhaustive list, as there are many more cryptocurrencies out there. But these are some of the most well-known and widely used ones.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 1160, 315, 2204, 4595, 315, 45074, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 49387, 320, 60218, 33395, 25, 578, 1176, 323, 1455, 1664, 22015, 27128, 11, 3549, 304, 220, 1049, 24, 555, 93252, 44329, 57960, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 36, 19041, 372, 320, 7780, 33395, 25, 362, 49063, 5452, 430, 20682, 279, 9886, 315, 7941, 17517, 323, 49063, 8522, 320, 67, 54702, 705, 11887, 304, 220, 679, 20, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 44944, 7307, 320, 43, 7905, 33395, 25, 362, 14734, 4791, 79697, 27128, 3549, 304, 220, 679, 16, 439, 264, 10819, 323, 23917, 10778, 311, 13428, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 49, 52264, 320, 55, 22394, 33395, 25, 362, 1972, 7394, 20547, 17516, 1887, 320, 5463, 16929, 8, 323, 11667, 9473, 323, 1323, 88291, 4009, 11, 11887, 304, 220, 679, 17, 627, 20, 13, 3146, 49387, 23139, 320, 33, 2198, 33395, 25, 362, 23243, 315, 13428, 11, 3549, 304, 220, 679, 22, 311, 5376, 279, 2565, 1404, 323, 2187, 369, 10819, 14463, 627, 21, 13, 3146, 5889, 5770, 320, 33393, 33395, 25, 362, 49063, 586, 18428, 323, 27128, 2447, 11, 11887, 304, 220, 679, 22, 449, 264, 5357, 389, 41329, 323, 94840, 627,