Output~2025-04-24 16:50:19.579252: [RequestOutput(request_id=508, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Name 6 components of an artificial neural network ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4076, 220, 21, 6956, 315, 459, 21075, 30828, 4009, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here are the 6 components of an artificial neural network:\n\n1. **Artificial Neurons (Nodes)**: These are the basic computing units of a neural network, inspired by biological neurons. Each node receives one or more inputs, performs a computation on those inputs, and then sends the output to other nodes.\n2. **Connections (Edges)**: These are the links between nodes, which allow them to communicate with each other. Each connection has a weight associated with it, which determines the strength of the signal transmitted between nodes.\n3. **Activation Functions**: These are mathematical functions that are applied to the output of each node to introduce non-linearity into the network. Common examples include sigmoid, ReLU (Rectified Linear Unit), and tanh.\n4. **Input Layer**: This is the first layer of nodes in the network, which receives the input data. The input layer is typically designed to match the format of the input data.\n5. **Hidden Layers**: These are the layers of nodes between the input layer and the output layer, where complex representations of the input data are built. Hidden layers can have multiple nodes, and each node applies an activation function to its output.\n6. **Output Layer**: This is the final layer of nodes in the network, which produces the output of the network. The output layer is typically designed to match the format of the desired output.\n\nThese six components work together to enable an artificial neural network to learn and make predictions or decisions based on input data.', token_ids=[8586, 527, 279, 220, 21, 6956, 315, 459, 21075, 30828, 4009, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 9470, 16895, 4275, 54769, 320, 12568, 33395, 25, 4314, 527, 279, 6913, 25213, 8316, 315, 264, 30828, 4009, 11, 14948, 555, 24156, 34313, 13, 9062, 2494, 21879, 832, 477, 810, 11374, 11, 27772, 264, 35547, 389, 1884, 11374, 11, 323, 1243, 22014, 279, 2612, 311, 1023, 7954, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 55851, 320, 42222, 33395, 25, 4314, 527, 279, 7902, 1990, 7954, 11, 902, 2187, 1124, 311, 19570, 449, 1855, 1023, 13, 9062, 3717, 706, 264, 4785, 5938, 449, 433, 11, 902, 27667, 279, 8333, 315, 279, 8450, 34699, 1990, 7954, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 62560, 24460, 96618, 4314, 527, 37072, 5865, 430, 527, 9435, 311, 279, 2612, 315, 1855, 2494, 311, 19678, 2536, 8614, 10981, 1139, 279, 4009, 13, 7874, 10507, 2997, 65990, 11, 1050, 24115, 320, 4515, 1908, 29363, 8113, 705, 323, 14531, 71, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 2566, 23570, 96618, 1115, 374, 279, 1176, 6324, 315, 7954, 304, 279, 4009, 11, 902, 21879, 279, 1988, 828, 13, 578, 1988, 6324, 374, 11383, 6319, 311, 2489, 279, 3645, 315, 279, 1988, 828, 627, 20, 13, 3146, 17964, 84922, 96618, 4314, 527, 279, 13931, 315, 7954, 1990, 279, 1988, 6324, 323, 279, 2612, 6324, 11, 1405, 6485, 44713, 315, 279, 1988, 828, 527, 5918, 13, 35342, 13931, 649, 617, 5361, 7954, 11, 323, 1855, 2494, 17208, 459, 15449, 734, 311, 1202, 2612, 627, 21, 13, 3146, 5207, 23570, 96618, 1115, 374, 279, 1620, 6324, 315, 7954, 304, 279, 4009, 11, 902, 19159, 279, 2612, 315, 279, 4009, 13, 578, 2612, 6324, 374, 11383, 6319, 311, 2489, 279, 3645, 315, 279, 12974, 2612, 382, 9673, 4848, 6956, 990, 3871, 311, 7431, 459, 21075, 30828, 4009, 311, 4048, 323, 1304,