opponent's hoop. In Baseball, the objective is to score runs by hitting the ball and running around the four bases.\n3. **Game duration**: American Football games are divided into four quarters, each lasting 15 minutes. Basketball games are divided into four quarters, each lasting 12 minutes. Baseball games are divided into nine innings, with each inning lasting around 3 hours.\n4. **Scoring system**: American Football uses a point system, with points awarded for touchdowns, field goals, and extra points. Basketball uses a point system, with points awarded for field goals and free throws. Baseball uses a run system, with runs awarded for each player who reaches home plate.\n5. **Popularity**: American Football is the most popular sport in the United States, with the Super Bowl being one of the most-watched television events. Basketball is the second most popular sport, with the NBA Finals being a highly anticipated event. Baseball is the third most popular sport, with the World Series being a beloved tradition.\n\nIn conclusion, while American Football, Basketball, and Baseball share some similarities, they each have unique characteristics that set them apart. Understanding these differences is essential for fans and players alike to appreciate the distinct nuances of each sport.", token_ids=[791, 3723, 4273, 374, 2162, 311, 264, 17226, 2134, 315, 10034, 11, 449, 2380, 315, 279, 1455, 5526, 6305, 1694, 3778, 21424, 11, 47589, 11, 323, 38258, 13, 6104, 814, 4430, 1063, 43874, 11, 1855, 10775, 706, 1202, 5016, 17910, 11, 5718, 11, 323, 8571, 2385, 13, 5810, 596, 264, 12593, 323, 13168, 315, 279, 2380, 10034, 1473, 334, 35502, 1385, 25, 57277, 16, 13, 3146, 14939, 6108, 96618, 2052, 2380, 10034, 527, 2128, 6108, 11, 449, 1403, 7411, 27260, 2403, 1855, 1023, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 40353, 488, 96618, 9062, 10775, 7612, 264, 1579, 2237, 315, 7106, 17479, 11, 8333, 11, 323, 49286, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 2645, 90467, 9293, 96618, 3623, 14576, 323, 4311, 1205, 311, 2274, 15174, 323,