Output~2025-04-24 16:52:06.281321: [RequestOutput(request_id=551, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: What is the history of the Tour de France? ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 3639, 374, 279, 3925, 315, 279, 14986, 409, 9822, 30, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='The Tour de France is one of the most prestigious and iconic cycling events in the world, with a rich history dating back to 1903. The first edition of the Tour de France was organized by the French newspaper L\'Auto, which was looking to create a cycling competition that would rival the Giro d\'Italia and the Vuelta a España.\n\nThe inaugural Tour de France took place from July 1 to July 19, 1903, and was won by Maurice Garin, a French cyclist who completed the 1,195-kilometer route in 122 hours and 49 minutes. The race was originally intended to be a six-day event, but it was extended to 15 days due to the popularity of the competition.\n\nOver the years, the Tour de France has undergone several changes, including the introduction of new stages, the elimination of others, and the addition of new teams and riders. The race has also been affected by various controversies, including doping scandals and crashes, which have led to the disqualification of several riders and teams.\n\nDespite these challenges, the Tour de France has continued to grow in popularity, attracting millions of spectators and viewers around the world. The race is now considered one of the most prestigious events in the world of cycling, and is often referred to as the "Grand Départ" of the cycling season.\n\nSome of the most notable winners of the Tour de France include:\n\n* Lance Armstrong (7 times)\n* Jacques Anquetil (5 times)\n* Bernard Hinault (5 times)\n* Eddy Merckx (5 times)\n* Greg LeMond (3 times)\n* Miguel Indurain (5 times)\n* Chris Froome (4 times)\n* Bradley Wiggins (1 time)\n* Alberto Contador (2 times)\n* Vincenzo Nibali (1 time)\n* Chris Froome (4 times)\n\nThe Tour de France is typically held over a period of three weeks in July, covering a distance of around 3,500 kilometers. The race is divided into 21 stages, with a mix of flat and mountainous terrain, as well as individual and team time trials. The winner of the Tour de France is awarded the coveted yellow jersey, which is worn by the leader of the general classification.\n\nOverall, the Tour de France is a beloved and iconic event that has been a part of French culture for over a century, and continues to captivate audiences around the world with its thrilling racing, stunning scenery, and rich history.', token_ids=[791, 14986, 409, 9822, 374, 832, 315, 279, 1455, 41385, 323, 27373, 33162, 4455, 304, 279, 1917, 11, 449, 264, 9257, 3925, 5029, 1203, 311, 220, 7028, 18, 13, 578, 1176, 14002, 315, 279, 14986, 409, 9822, 574, 17057, 555, 279, 8753, 17222, 445, 6, 13556, 11, 902, 574, 3411, 311, 1893, 264, 33162, 10937, 430, 1053, 21425, 279, 480, 8869, 294, 75750, 19379, 323, 279, 650, 4088, 2629, 264, 57608, 382, 791, 54559, 14986, 409, 9822, 3952, 2035, 505, 5887, 220, 16, 311, 5887, 220, 777, 11, 220, 7028, 18, 11, 323, 574, 2834, 555, 68529, 12471, 258, 11, 264, 8753, 81131, 889, 8308, 279, 220, 16, 11, 6280, 12934, 321, 21037, 6149, 304, 220, 8259, 4207, 323, 220, 2491, 4520, 13, 578, 7102, 574, 13517, 10825, 311, 387, 264, 4848, 11477, 1567, 11, 719, 433, 574, 11838, 311, 220, 868, 2919, 4245, 311, 279, 23354, 315, 279, 10937, 382, 1959, 279, 1667, 11, 279, 14986, 409, 9822, 706, 64238, 3892, 4442, 1