Output~2025-04-24 16:55:44.239145: [RequestOutput(request_id=649, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Hypothesize why Australia has over 140 snake species. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 39515, 78, 27985, 3249, 8494, 706, 927, 220, 6860, 26332, 9606, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Australia's unique geography and climate have contributed to the evolution of a diverse range of snake species. The country's isolation from other continents for millions of years has allowed its native snakes to adapt and thrive in a variety of environments.\n\nOne reason for the high number of snake species in Australia is the country's vast and varied geography. From the arid deserts of the Outback to the lush rainforests of the east coast, Australia's diverse landscapes provide a range of habitats for snakes to inhabit. Each of these habitats has its own unique set of conditions, such as temperature, humidity, and vegetation, that have driven the evolution of different snake species.\n\nAnother factor that has contributed to the high number of snake species in Australia is the country's relatively stable climate. Unlike many other parts of the world, Australia has not experienced significant changes in climate over the past few million years, which has allowed its native snakes to evolve and thrive without the need to adapt to dramatic changes in their environment.\n\nAdditionally, Australia's isolation from other continents has meant that its snakes have not been subject to the same level of competition and predation as snakes in other parts of the world. This has allowed them to evolve in relative peace, without the need to compete with other species for resources or territory.\n\nFinally, Australia's unique geology has also played a role in the evolution of its snake species. The country's ancient rocks and soil have provided a rich source of nutrients and minerals, which have supported the growth of a diverse range of plants and animals, including snakes.\n\nIn conclusion, the combination of Australia's unique geography, stable climate, lack of competition, and rich geology have all contributed to the evolution of over 140 species of snakes in the country.", token_ids=[49137, 596, 5016, 54242, 323, 10182, 617, 20162, 311, 279, 15740, 315, 264, 17226, 2134, 315, 26332, 9606, 13, 578, 3224, 596, 31398, 505, 1023, 66959, 369, 11990, 315, 1667, 706, 5535, 1202, 10068, 57196, 311, 10737, 323, 41972, 304, 264, 8205, 315, 22484, 382, 4054, 2944, 369, 279, 1579, 1396, 315, 26332, 9606, 304, 8494, 374, 279, 3224, 596, 13057, 323, 28830, 54242, 13, 5659, 279, 802, 307, 951, 15916, 315, 279, 4470, 1445, 311, 279, 58367, 11422, 1348, 37379, 315, 279, 11226, 13962, 11, 8494, 596, 17226, 55890, 3493, 264, 2134, 315, 71699, 369, 57196, 311, 33427, 13, 9062, 315, 1521, 71699, 706, 1202, 1866, 5016, 743, 315, 4787, 11, 1778, 439, 9499, 11, 38193, 11, 323, 54832, 11, 430, 617, 16625, 279, 15740, 315, 2204, 26332, 9606, 382, 14364, 8331, 430, 706, 20162, 311, 279, 1579, 1396, 315, 26332, 9606, 304, 8494, 374, 279, 3224, 596, 12309, 15528, 10182, 13, 27140, 1690, 1023, 5596, 315, 279, 1917, 11, 8494, 706, 539, 10534, 5199, 4442, 304, 10182, 927, 279, 3347, 2478, 3610, 1667, 11, 902, 706, 5535, 1202, 10068, 57196, 311, 38680, 323, 41972, 2085, 279, 1205, 311, 10737, 311, 22520, 4442, 304, 872, 4676, 382, 50674, 11, 8494, 596, 31398, 505, 1023, 66959, 706, 8967, 430, 1202, 57196, 617, 539, 1027, 3917, 311, 279, 1890, 2237, 315, 10937, 3