Output~2025-04-24 16:57:54.969512: [RequestOutput(request_id=690, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write an algorithm to find the minimum element in an array. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 459, 12384, 311, 1505, 279, 8187, 2449, 304, 459, 1358, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a simple algorithm to find the minimum element in an array:\n\n**Algorithm:**\n\n1. Initialize a variable `min` to the first element of the array.\n2. Iterate through the array starting from the second element (index 1) to the last element.\n3. For each element, compare it with the current `min` value.\n4. If the current element is smaller than `min`, update `min` with the current element.\n5. After iterating through the entire array, `min` will hold the smallest element in the array.\n6. Return the value of `min`.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n```\nfunction findMin(arr):\n    min = arr[0]\n    for i = 1 to arr.length - 1:\n        if arr[i] < min:\n            min = arr[i]\n    return min\n```\n**Example:**\n\nInput array: `[3, 1, 4, 2, 5, 6]`\n\n1. Initialize `min` to `3`.\n2. Iterate through the array:\n\t* `i = 1`, `arr[i] = 1`, `1 < 3`, so update `min` to `1`.\n\t* `i = 2`, `arr[i] = 4`, `4 > 1`, no update.\n\t* `i = 3`, `arr[i] = 2`, `2 < 1`, update `min` to `2`.\n\t* `i = 4`, `arr[i] = 5`, `5 > 2`, no update.\n\t* `i = 5`, `arr[i] = 6`, `6 > 2`, no update.\n3. Return `min`, which is `2`.\n\nThe minimum element in the array is `2`.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 4382, 12384, 311, 1505, 279, 8187, 2449, 304, 459, 1358, 1473, 334, 28947, 25, 57277, 16, 13, 9185, 264, 3977, 1595, 1083, 63, 311, 279, 1176, 2449, 315, 279, 1358, 627, 17, 13, 55440, 1555, 279, 1358, 6041, 505, 279, 2132, 2449, 320, 1275, 220, 16, 8, 311, 279, 1566, 2449, 627, 18, 13, 1789, 1855, 2449, 11, 9616, 433, 449, 279, 1510, 1595, 1083, 63, 907, 627, 19, 13, 1442, 279, 1510, 2449, 374, 9333, 1109, 1595, 1083, 7964, 2713, 1595, 1083, 63, 449, 279, 1510, 2449, 627, 20, 13, 4740, 88335, 1555, 279, 4553, 1358, 11, 1595, 1083, 63, 690, 3412, 279, 25655, 2449, 304, 279, 1358, 627, 21, 13, 3494, 279, 907, 315, 1595, 1083, 63438, 334, 47, 40512, 44788, 25, 1035, 14196, 4077, 1723, 1505, 6349, 11179, 997, 262, 1332, 284, 2961, 58, 15, 933, 262, 369, 602, 284, 220, 16, 311, 2961, 1996, 482, 220, 16, 512, 286, 422, 2961, 1004, 60, 366, 1332, 512, 310, 1332, 284, 2961, 1004, 933, 262, 471, 1332, 198, 14196, 4077, 334, 13617, 25, 57277, 2566, 1358, 25, 78744, 18, 11, 220, 16, 11, 220, 19, 11, 220, 17, 11, 220, 20, 11, 220, 21, 60, 19884, 16, 13, 9185, 1595, 1083, 63, 311, 1595, 18, 19154, 17, 13, 55440, 1555, 279, 1358, 512, 197, 9, 1595, 72, 284, 220, 16, 7964, 1595, 1138, 1004, 60, 284, 220, 16, 7964, 1595, 16, 366, 220, 18, 7964, 779, 2713, 1595, 1083, 63, 311, 1595, 16, 19154, 197, 9, 1595, 72, 284, 220, 17, 7964, 1595, 1138, 1004, 60, 284, 220, 19, 7964, 1595, 19, 871, 220, 16, 7964, 912, 2713, 627, 197, 9, 1595, 72, 284, 220, 18, 7964, 1595, 1138, 1004, 60, 284, 220, 17, 7964, 1595, 17, 366, 220, 16, 7964, 2713, 1595, 1083, 63, 311, 1595, 17, 19154, 197, 9, 1595, 72, 284, 220, 19, 7964, 1595, 1138, 1004, 60, 284, 220, 20, 7964, 1595, 20, 871, 220, 17, 7964, 912, 2713, 627, 197, 9, 1595, 72, 284, 220, 20, 7964, 1595, 1138, 1004, 60, 284, 220, 21, 7964, 1595, 21, 871, 220, 17, 7964, 912, 2713, 627, 18, 13, 3494, 1595, 1083, 7964, 902, 374, 1595, 17, 63438, 791, 8187, 2449, 304, 279, 1358, 374, 1595, 17, 29687, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None,