Output~2025-04-24 16:59:00.328360: [RequestOutput(request_id=714, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Create a plan for a budget-friendly Thanksgiving meal. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4324, 264, 3197, 369, 264, 8199, 22658, 37250, 15496, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here's a plan for a budget-friendly Thanksgiving meal:\n\n**Menu:**\n\n* Main Course: Roasted Turkey Breast with Gravy\n* Side Dishes:\n\t+ Mashed Potatoes\n\t+ Green Bean Casserole\n\t+ Stuffing (using stale bread and vegetables)\n\t+ Cranberry Sauce (homemade using fresh or frozen cranberries)\n* Dessert: Pumpkin Pie (homemade using canned pumpkin puree and store-bought crust)\n\n**Budget Breakdown:**\n\n* Turkey Breast (4-5 lbs): $10-$12\n* Potatoes (4-5): $1.50-$2\n* Green Beans (1 lb): $1.50-$2\n* Stuffing ingredients (bread, vegetables, herbs): $2-$3\n* Cranberries (fresh or frozen): $2-$3\n* Pumpkin puree (canned): $1-$2\n* Pie crust (store-bought): $2-$3\n* Spices and seasonings: $1-$2\n* Total: $25-$35\n\n**Tips for Saving Money:**\n\n* Buy a smaller turkey breast to reduce waste and save on food costs.\n* Use leftover bread to make stuffing, reducing the need for expensive bread crumbs.\n* Opt for canned pumpkin puree instead of fresh pumpkin.\n* Make your own cranberry sauce using fresh or frozen cranberries instead of store-bought.\n* Use store-bought pie crust to save time and money.\n* Plan ahead and make as much as you can ahead of time to reduce last-minute expenses.\n\n**Timeline:**\n\n* 1 week before Thanksgiving: Make the cranberry sauce and store it in the fridge.\n* 2-3 days before Thanksgiving: Prepare the stuffing and store it in the fridge.\n* Thanksgiving Day: Roast the turkey breast, prepare the mashed potatoes, green bean casserole, and pumpkin pie.\n* After Thanksgiving: Use leftover turkey to make sandwiches or soups, and freeze any leftover sides for future meals.\n\n**Tips for Cooking:**\n\n* Use a slow cooker to cook the turkey breast and make the mashed potatoes.\n* Make the green bean casserole ahead of time and refrigerate or freeze until ready to bake.\n* Use a store-bought pie crust to make the pumpkin pie, or make your own crust using a simple recipe.\n* Don't be afraid to get creative and adjust the menu to suit your tastes and dietary needs.\n\nBy following this plan, you can enjoy a delicious and budget-friendly Thanksgiving meal without breaking", token_ids=[8586, 596, 264, 3197, 369, 264, 8199, 22658, 37250, 15496, 1473, 334, 3598, 25, 57277, 9, 4802, 17026, 25, 12093, 15386, 17442, 57598, 449, 2895, 5781, 198, 9, 17072, 423, 21168, 512, 197, 10, 386, 13883, 14020, 20798, 198, 197, 10, 7997, 34823, 26520, 261, 1286, 198, 197, 10, 46586, 287, 320, 985, 51451, 16385, 323, 24822, 340, 197, 10, 67530, 15717, 61276, 320, 35940, 29532, 1701, 7878, 477, 20268, 70637, 36989, 340, 9, 70596, 531, 25, 76357, 41097, 320, 35940, 29532, 1701, 64114, 50625, 10748, 68, 323, 3637, 1481, 2509, 40712, 696, 334, 64001, 15996, 2996, 25, 57277, 9, 17442, 57598, 320, 19, 12, 20, 29160, 1680, 400, 605, 22104, 717, 198, 9, 14020, 20798, 320, 19, 12, 20, 1680, 400, 16, 13, 1135, 22104, 17, 198, 9, 7997, 81836, 320, 16, 19398, 1680, 400, 16, 13, 1135, 22104, 17, 198, 9, 46586, 287, 14293, 320, 48616, 11, 24822, 11, 42393, 1680, 400, 17, 22104, 18, 198, 9, 67530, 36989, 320, 72408, 477, 20268, 1680, 400, 17, 22104, 18, 198, 9, 76357, 10748, 68, 320, 66, 7443, 1680, 400, 16, 22104, 17, 198, 9, 41097, 40712, 320, 4412,