Output~2025-04-24 17:00:01.041150: [RequestOutput(request_id=750, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Describe a process of cleaning silverware. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 61885, 264, 1920, 315, 16204, 15310, 1698, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is a response that completes the request:\n\n**Cleaning Silverware: A Step-by-Step Guide**\n\nCleaning silverware is an essential task to maintain its shine and prevent tarnish. Here's a simple and effective process to clean your silverware:\n\n**Step 1: Gather Materials**\n\n* Silverware to be cleaned\n* Mild dish soap\n* Warm water\n* Soft cloth or sponge\n* Silver polish (optional)\n* Dry cloth for drying\n\n**Step 2: Remove Large Food Particles**\n\n* Rinse the silverware under warm running water to remove any large food particles.\n* Use a soft cloth or sponge to wipe away any remaining debris.\n\n**Step 3: Mix Soap and Water**\n\n* In a bowl, mix 1 tablespoon of mild dish soap with 1 cup of warm water.\n* Stir the solution until the soap is fully dissolved.\n\n**Step 4: Soak the Silverware**\n\n* Submerge the silverware in the soapy water mixture and let it soak for 15-30 minutes.\n* This will help loosen any stubborn food residue and tarnish.\n\n**Step 5: Scrub the Silverware**\n\n* Use a soft cloth or sponge to gently scrub each piece of silverware, paying attention to any areas with heavy tarnish or food residue.\n* Avoid using abrasive materials or harsh chemicals, as they can damage the silver.\n\n**Step 6: Rinse and Dry**\n\n* Rinse the silverware under warm running water to remove any soap residue.\n* Use a dry cloth to dry each piece of silverware, paying extra attention to crevices and handles.\n\n**Step 7: Polish (Optional)**\n\n* If you want to add an extra layer of shine to your silverware, use a silver polish according to the manufacturer's instructions.\n* Apply the polish to a soft cloth and rub it onto the silverware in a circular motion.\n* Buff the silverware with a clean, dry cloth to remove any excess polish.\n\n**Step 8: Store the Silverware**\n\n* Once the silverware is clean and dry, store it in a cool, dry place to prevent tarnish.\n\nBy following these simple steps, you can keep your silverware clean, shiny, and in great condition.", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 2077, 430, 45695, 279, 1715, 1473, 334, 98281, 15347, 1698, 25, 362, 15166, 14656, 12, 8468, 13002, 57277, 98281, 15310, 1698, 374, 459, 7718, 3465, 311, 10519, 1202, 33505, 323, 5471, 87580, 819, 13, 5810, 596, 264, 4382, 323, 7524, 1920, 311, 4335, 701, 15310, 1698, 1473, 334, 8468, 220, 16, 25, 50095, 32009, 57277, 9, 15347, 1698, 311, 387, 28822, 198, 9, 61289, 12269, 27883, 198, 9, 46863, 3090, 198, 9, 25046, 28392, 477, 69448, 198, 9, 15347, 45129, 320, 13099, 340, 9, 31941, 28392, 369, 46479, 271, 334, 8468, 220, 17, 25, 11016, 20902, 12369, 3744, 4440, 57277, 9, 58468, 325, 279, 15310, 1698, 1234, 8369, 4401, 3090, 311, 4148, 904, 3544, 3691, 19252, 627, 9, 5560, 264, 8579, 28392, 477, 69448, 311, 40194, 3201, 904, 9861, 35098, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 18, 25, 19771, 61731, 323, 10164, 57277, 9, 763, 264, 19763, 11, 6651, 220, 16, 62611, 315, 23900, 12269, 27883, 449, 220, 16, 10747, 315, 8369, 3090, 627, 9, 65292, 279, 6425, 3156, 279, 27883, 374, 7373, 56767, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 19, 25, 2100, 587, 279, 15347, 1698, 57277, 9, 3804, 19590, 279, 15310, 1698, 304, 279, 779, 9864, 3090, 21655, 323, 1095, 433, 61792, 369, 220, 868, 12, 966, 4520, 627, 9, 1115, 6