Output~2025-04-24 17:01:34.537525: [RequestOutput(request_id=793, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Explain the concept of information retrieval. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 83017, 279, 7434, 315, 2038, 57470, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Information retrieval (IR) is the process of obtaining relevant information from a large collection of data, such as a database, library, or the internet. It involves searching for specific information, filtering out irrelevant data, and presenting the most relevant results to the user.\n\nThe goal of information retrieval is to provide users with accurate and relevant information that meets their needs and queries. This is achieved through various techniques, including:\n\n1. **Indexing**: Creating an index of keywords, phrases, and concepts to facilitate fast and efficient searching.\n2. **Query processing**: Processing user queries, such as keywords, phrases, or natural language, to identify relevant documents or data.\n3. **Retrieval**: Retrieving relevant documents or data from the indexed collection based on the query.\n4. **Ranking**: Ranking the retrieved documents or data in order of relevance, based on factors such as keyword frequency, document length, and user preferences.\n5. **Presentation**: Presenting the retrieved and ranked results to the user, often in a user-friendly format, such as a list of search results or a summary of the most relevant information.\n\nInformation retrieval is a crucial aspect of many applications, including:\n\n1. **Search engines**: Web search engines, such as Google, use IR to retrieve relevant web pages from the internet.\n2. **Databases**: Database systems use IR to retrieve specific data records or documents from a large collection of data.\n3. **Document management systems**: Document management systems use IR to retrieve specific documents or files from a large collection of documents.\n4. **Recommendation systems**: Recommendation systems use IR to suggest products, movies, or music based on user preferences and behavior.\n\nIn summary, information retrieval is the process of searching, filtering, and presenting relevant information from a large collection of data to meet the needs of users.', token_ids=[15218, 57470, 320, 2871, 8, 374, 279, 1920, 315, 19546, 9959, 2038, 505, 264, 3544, 4526, 315, 828, 11, 1778, 439, 264, 4729, 11, 6875, 11, 477, 279, 7757, 13, 1102, 18065, 15389, 369, 3230, 2038, 11, 30770, 704, 40815, 828, 11, 323, 32644, 279, 1455, 9959, 3135, 311, 279, 1217, 382, 791, 5915, 315, 2038, 57470, 374, 311, 3493, 3932, 449, 13687, 323, 9959, 2038, 430, 20628, 872, 3966, 323, 20126, 13, 1115, 374, 17427, 1555, 5370, 12823, 11, 2737, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 1581, 287, 96618, 32406, 459, 1963, 315, 21513, 11, 32847, 11, 323, 19476, 311, 28696, 5043, 323, 11297, 15389, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 2929, 8863, 96618, 29225, 1217, 20126, 11, 1778, 439, 21513, 11, 32847, 11, 477, 5933, 4221, 11, 311, 10765, 9959, 9477, 477, 828, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 12289, 7379, 838, 96618, 20035, 4504, 9959, 9477, 477, 828, 505, 279, 31681, 4526, 3196, 389, 279, 3319, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 23366, 287, 96618, 65175, 279, 31503, 9477, 477, 828, 304, 2015, 315, 41961, 11, 3196, 389, 9547, 1778, 439, 16570, 11900, 11, 2246, 3160, 11, 323, 1217, 19882, 627, 20, 13, 3146, 56339, 96618, 27740, 287, 279, 31503, 323, 21682, 3135, 311, 279, 1217, 11, 3629, 304, 264, 1217, 22658, 3645, 11, 1778, 439, 264, 1160, 315, 2778, 3135, 477, 264, 12399, 3