Output~2025-04-24 17:01:51.209325: [RequestOutput(request_id=798, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: How do you create a pivot table in Excel? ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 2650, 656, 499, 1893, 264, 27137, 2007, 304, 21705, 30, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Creating a pivot table in Excel is a powerful way to summarize and analyze large datasets. Here\'s a step-by-step guide on how to create a pivot table in Excel:\n\n**Step 1: Select the data range**\n\nFirst, select the entire dataset that you want to analyze. Make sure the data is organized in a table format with headers in the first row.\n\n**Step 2: Go to the "Insert" tab**\n\nClick on the "Insert" tab in the ribbon at the top of the Excel window.\n\n**Step 3: Click on "PivotTable"**\n\nIn the "Tables" group, click on the "PivotTable" button.\n\n**Step 4: Choose a cell location**\n\nIn the "Create PivotTable" dialog box, select a cell where you want to place the pivot table. You can choose a cell in a new worksheet or an existing one.\n\n**Step 5: Click "OK"**\n\nClick "OK" to create the pivot table.\n\n**Step 6: Drag fields to the "Rows" and "Columns" areas**\n\nIn the "PivotTable Fields" pane, drag the fields you want to use in your pivot table to the "Rows" and "Columns" areas. You can drag multiple fields to create a hierarchical structure.\n\n**Step 7: Drag fields to the "Values" area**\n\nDrag the fields you want to summarize to the "Values" area. You can choose from various aggregation functions such as Sum, Average, Count, and more.\n\n**Step 8: Customize the pivot table**\n\nYou can customize the pivot table by changing the layout, formatting, and filtering options. You can also use the "PivotTable Tools" tab to add more features such as charts, slicers, and filters.\n\n**Step 9: Refresh the pivot table**\n\nTo update the pivot table with new data, click on the "Refresh" button in the "PivotTable Tools" tab or press F5.\n\nThat\'s it! With these steps, you\'ve created a pivot table in Excel. You can now use it to analyze and summarize your data in a more efficient and effective way.', token_ids=[26021, 264, 27137, 2007, 304, 21705, 374, 264, 8147, 1648, 311, 63179, 323, 24564, 3544, 30525, 13, 5810, 596, 264, 3094, 14656, 30308, 8641, 389, 1268, 311, 1893, 264, 27137, 2007, 304, 21705, 1473, 334, 8468, 220, 16, 25, 8593, 279, 828, 2134, 57277, 5451, 11, 3373, 279, 4553, 10550, 430, 499, 1390, 311, 24564, 13, 7557, 2771, 279, 828, 374, 17057, 304, 264, 2007, 3645, 449, 7247, 304, 279, 1176, 2872, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 17, 25, 6122, 311, 279, 330, 14099, 1, 5769, 57277, 2677, 389, 279, 330, 14099, 1, 5769, 304, 279, 45667, 520, 279, 1948, 315, 279, 21705, 3321, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 18, 25, 9369, 389, 330, 47, 16471, 2620, 1, 57277, 644, 279, 330, 22409, 1, 1912, 11, 4299, 389, 279, 330, 47, 16471, 2620, 1, 3215, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 19, 25, 22991, 264, 2849, 3813, 57277, 644, 279, 330, 4110, 98993, 2620, 1, 7402, 3830, 11, 3373, 264, 2849, 1405, 499, 1390, 311, 2035, 279, 27137, 2007, 13, 1472, 649, 5268, 264, 2849, 304, 264, 502, 37736, 477, 459, 6484, 832, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 20, 25, 9369, 330, 4012, 1, 57277, 2677, 330, 4012, 1, 311, 1893, 279, 27137, 2007, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 21, 25, 25903, 5151, 311, 279, 330, 9201, 1, 323, 330, 14292, 1, 5789, 57277, 644, 279, 330, 47, 16471, 2620, 25599, 1, 38422, 11, 11161, 279, 5151, 499, 1390, 311, 1005, 304, 701, 27137, 2007, 311, 279, 330, 9201, 1, 323, 330, 14292, 1, 5789, 13, 1472, 649, 11