Output~2025-04-24 17:05:04.825752: [RequestOutput(request_id=860, prompt='<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{\'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Summarize the book "The Goldfinch" by Donna Tartt ### Response:\'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n', prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 8279, 5730, 553, 279, 2363, 330, 791, 7573, 5589, 331, 1, 555, 47863, 78641, 83, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a summary of "The Goldfinch" by Donna Tartt:\n\n"The Goldfinch" is a novel by Donna Tartt that tells the story of Theo Decker, a young boy who survives a terrorist bombing at the Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York City that kills his mother. The bombing occurs when Theo is 13 years old, and he is forced to flee the scene, leaving behind his mother\'s body and the famous painting "The Goldfinch" by Carel Fabritius.\n\nTheo is taken in by a wealthy family, the Barbours, who adopt him as their own. However, he struggles to adjust to his new life and is haunted by the trauma of the bombing and the loss of his mother. He becomes obsessed with the painting, which he believes is a symbol of his mother\'s love and a connection to her.\n\nAs Theo grows older, he becomes increasingly withdrawn and isolated, struggling to form meaningful relationships with others. He is drawn to a group of outcasts and misfits, including a young woman named Pippa and a wealthy and troubled young man named Boris. Together, they form a tight-knit group that is bound together by their shared experiences and outsider status.\n\nThroughout the novel, Tartt explores themes of trauma, grief, and the power of art to transcend time and mortality. The novel is a sweeping and epic tale that spans decades, following Theo\'s journey from childhood to adulthood as he grapples with the consequences of his past and the secrets that have been kept from him.\n\nUltimately, "The Goldfinch" is a novel about the human search for meaning and connection in a chaotic and often cruel world. It is a powerful and moving exploration of the human condition, and a testament to the enduring power of art to bring people together and transcend the boundaries of time and space.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 12399, 315, 330, 791, 7573, 5589, 331, 1, 555, 47863, 78641, 83, 1473, 10227, 7573, 5589, 331, 1, 374, 264, 11775, 555, 47863, 78641, 83, 430, 10975, 279, 3446, 315, 85237, 1611, 15512, 11, 264, 3995, 8334, 889, 83417, 264, 20320, 37431, 520, 279, 45878, 16730, 315, 5277, 304, 1561, 4356, 4409, 430, 29910, 813, 6691, 13, 578, 37431, 13980, 994, 85237, 374, 220, 1032, 1667, 2362, 11, 323, 568, 374, 9770, 311, 28500, 279, 6237, 11, 9564, 4920, 813, 6691, 596, 2547, 323, 279, 11495, 19354, 330, 791, 7573, 5589, 331, 1, 555, 10852, 75, 19797, 1018, 9334, 382, 110798, 374, 4529, 304, 555, 264, 28994, 3070, 11, 279, 47142, 2530, 11, 889, 11142, 1461, 439, 872, 1866, 13, 4452, 11, 568, 28970, 311, 7652, 311, 813, 502, 2324, 323, 374, 57775, 555, 279, 30988, 315, 279, 37431, 323, 279, 4814, 315, 813, 6691, 13, 1283, 9221, 44898, 449, 279, 19354, 11, 902, 568, 13919, 374, 264, 7891, 315, 813, 6691, 596, 3021, 323, 264, 3717, 311, 1077, 382, 2170, 85237, 28815, 9191, 11, 568, 9221, 15098, 50682, 323, 25181, 11, 20558, 311, 1376, 23222, 12135, 449, 3885, 13, 1283, 374, 15107, 311, 264, 1912, 315, 704, 51134, 323, 5906, 30322, 11, 2737, 264, 3995, 5333, 7086, 393, 2877, 64, 323, 264, 28994, 323, 42132, 3995, 893, 7086, 52771, 13, 32255, 11, 814, 1376, 264, 10508, 12934, 45168, 1912, 430, 374, 6965, 3871, 555, 872, 6222, 11704, 323, 75683, 2704, 382, 60105, 279, 11775, 11