Output~2025-04-24 17:10:52.768820: [RequestOutput(request_id=1006, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Find the smallest value of x that satisfies the equation |3x+7|=26. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 7531, 279, 25655, 907, 315, 865, 430, 69001, 279, 24524, 765, 18, 87, 10, 22, 88903, 1627, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='To find the smallest value of x that satisfies the equation |3x+7|=26, we can start by isolating the absolute value expression:\n\n|3x+7| = 26\n\nThis equation is equivalent to:\n\n3x + 7 = 26 or 3x + 7 = -26\n\nNow, we can solve each equation separately:\n\nCase 1: 3x + 7 = 26\n\nSubtract 7 from both sides:\n\n3x = 19\n\nDivide both sides by 3:\n\nx = 19/3\n\nx = 6.33\n\nCase 2: 3x + 7 = -26\n\nSubtract 7 from both sides:\n\n3x = -33\n\nDivide both sides by 3:\n\nx = -11\n\nSince we are looking for the smallest value of x, we choose the solution x = -11.\n\nTherefore, the smallest value of x that satisfies the equation |3x+7|=26 is x = -11.', token_ids=[1271, 1505, 279, 25655, 907, 315, 865, 430, 69001, 279, 24524, 765, 18, 87, 10, 22, 88903, 1627, 11, 584, 649, 1212, 555, 13399, 1113, 279, 10973, 907, 7645, 1473, 91, 18, 87, 10, 22, 91, 284, 220, 1627, 271, 2028, 24524, 374, 13890, 311, 1473, 18, 87, 489, 220, 22, 284, 220, 1627, 477, 220, 18, 87, 489, 220, 22, 284, 482, 1627, 271, 7184, 11, 584, 649, 11886, 1855, 24524, 26214, 1473, 4301, 220, 16, 25, 220, 18, 87, 489, 220, 22, 284, 220, 1627, 271, 3214, 2193, 220, 22