r current world has made significant progress in promoting human rights, democracy, and international cooperation.\n\n**Technology:**\n\nThe technology in the Star Wars universe is often more advanced than what we have today, with capabilities such as:\n\n1. Faster-than-light travel: The ability to travel across vast distances in a relatively short period is a hallmark of the Star Wars universe. This technology is not yet possible in our world, but scientists are exploring the concept of warp drives and other methods to achieve faster-than-light travel.\n2. Advanced computing: The Star Wars universe features advanced computers and artificial intelligence, such as the droids C-3PO and R2-D2. While our computers are more powerful and widespread, the Star Wars universe's AI systems are more advanced in terms of their ability to interact with humans and make decisions.\n3. Energy weapons: The Star Wars universe features a range of energy-based weapons, including blasters, lightsabers, and Death Stars. While we have developed more advanced energy weapons, such as lasers and particle beams, they are not yet as widespread or powerful as those in the Star Wars universe.\n4. Medical technology: The Star Wars universe features advanced medical technology, including bacta tanks, which can heal wounds and regenerate tissue. While we have made significant progress in medical technology, we have not yet developed the ability to regenerate tissue or heal wounds as quickly and effectively as the Star Wars universe.\n\n**Comparison to our current world:**\n\nIn terms of the level of civilization and technology, the Star Wars universe is more advanced in some", token_ids=[36, 26591, 1113, 279, 2237, 315, 36017, 323, 5557, 304, 279, 7834, 15317, 15861, 374, 264, 27387, 3465, 13, 578, 7834, 15317, 34261, 374, 264, 13057, 323, 17226, 2035, 11, 449, 5370, 33975, 323, 34775, 430, 617, 8040, 520, 2204, 7969, 13, 4452, 11, 369, 279, 7580, 315, 420, 16865, 11, 358, 690, 5357, 389, 279, 1925,