\n3. We iterate through the curse words and replace each one in the input string with a string of asterisks (`*`) of the same length as the curse word.\n4. We return the censored string.\n\nNote that this function assumes that the curse words are stored in a single column called `WORD` in the `CURSE_WORDS_TABLE` table, and that the input string is a single string. You may need to modify the function to accommodate different table and column names, or to handle multiple input strings.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 13325, 734, 430, 272, 27627, 41100, 4339, 4871, 264, 925, 555, 4737, 279, 41100, 4339, 505, 459, 8029, 4729, 512, 14196, 4077, 475, 22775, 18, 271, 755, 40065, 19492, 325, 19518, 5498, 3991, 997, 262, 674, 13313, 311, 279, 4729, 198, 262, 4635, 284, 22775, 18, 11034, 493, 2407, 325, 19518, 7221, 1329, 262, 8291, 284, 4635, 21361, 2892, 262, 674, 11615, 279, 41100, 4339, 505, 279, 4729, 198, 262, 8291, 7925, 446, 4963, 37991, 4393, 19058, 937, 89521, 16424, 1158, 262, 41100, 19518, 284, 510, 654, 58, 15, 60, 369, 2872, 304, 8291, 43230, 93208, 262, 674, 356, 3890, 279, 41100, 4339, 304, 279, 1988, 925, 198, 262, 369, 41100, 13843, 304, 41100, 19518, 512, 286, 1988, 3991, 284, 1988, 3991, 7125, 18053, 325, 13843, 11, 31801, 353, 2479, 18053, 325, 13843, 4489, 262, 674, 3494, 279, 272, 56878, 925, 198, 262, 471, 1988, 3991, 198, 14196, 4077, 8586, 596, 459, 16540, 315, 279, 2082, 1473, 16, 13, 1226, 4667, 311, 279, 29434, 4729, 1701, 279, 1595, 38142, 18, 63, 6875, 627, 17, 13, 1226, 3319, 279, 1595, 39891, 937, 89521, 16424, 63, 2007, 323, 17622, 279, 1160, 315, 41100, 4339, 627, 18, 13, 1226, 30729, 1555, 279, 41100, 4339, 323, 8454, 1855, 832, 304, 279, 1988, 925, 449, 264, 925, 315, 35037, 93934, 29754, 9, 33981, 315, 279, 1890, 3160, 439, 279, 41100, 3492, 627, 19, 13, 1226, 471, 279, 272, 56878, 925, 382, 9290, 430, 420, 734, 22204, 430, 279, 41100, 4339, 527, 9967, 304, 264, 3254, 3330, 2663, 1595, 7375, 63, 304, 279, 1595, 39891, 937, 89521, 16424, 63, 