Output~2025-04-24 17:15:50.039243: [RequestOutput(request_id=1159, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Provide an example of a situation to go with the example. ### Input: Person A always blames Person B for their mistakes. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 40665, 459, 3187, 315, 264, 6671, 311, 733, 449, 279, 3187, 13, 17010, 5688, 25, 7508, 362, 2744, 86890, 7508, 426, 369, 872, 21294, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here's an example of a situation that illustrates the instruction:\n\n**Example Situation:**\n\nPerson A, a software developer, is working on a project with Person B, a designer. They are tasked with creating a new mobile app for a popular restaurant chain. Person A is responsible for writing the code, while Person B is in charge of designing the user interface.\n\nDuring the development process, Person A accidentally introduces a bug that causes the app to crash frequently. When the project manager, Sarah, points out the issue, Person A immediately blames Person B for the mistake, claiming that the design is flawed and that's why the app is malfunctioning.\n\nSarah is frustrated with Person A's constant blaming and decides to have a meeting with both of them to discuss the issue. In the meeting, Person A continues to shift the blame to Person B, saying that the design is too complex and that's why the code is having trouble functioning properly.\n\n**Example Response:**\n\nThis situation illustrates how Person A always blames Person B for their mistakes. Despite being responsible for writing the code, Person A deflects the blame to Person B, claiming that the design is the root of the problem. This behavior not only creates tension in the team but also hinders the problem-solving process, as Person B feels defensive and unwilling to work together to find a solution.", token_ids=[8586, 596, 459, 3187, 315, 264, 6671, 430, 46480, 279, 7754, 1473, 334, 13617, 69478, 25, 57277, 10909, 362, 11, 264, 3241, 16131, 11, 374, 3318, 389, 264, 2447, 449, 7508, 426, 11, 264, 15034, 13, 2435, 527, 51920, 449, 6968, 264, 502, 6505, 917, 369, 264, 5526, 10960, 8957, 13, 7508, 362, 374, 8647, 369, 4477, 279, 2082, 11, 1418, 7508, 426, 374, 304, 6900, 315, 30829, 279, 1217, 3834, 382, 16397, 279, 4500, 1920, 11, 7508, 362, 33484, 40019, 264, 10077, 430, 11384, 279, 917, 311, 10121, 14134, 13, 3277, 279, 2447, 6783, 11, 21077, 11, 3585, 704, 279, 4360, 11, 7508, 362, 7214, 86890, 7508, 426, 369, 279, 16930, 11, 21039, 430, 279, 2955, 374, 48008, 323, 430, 596, 3249, 279, 917, 374, 72287, 287, 382, 54183, 374, 33630, 449, 7508, 362, 596, 6926, 59771, 323, 28727, 311, 617, 264, 6574, 449, 2225, 315, 1124, 311, 4358, 279, 4360, 13, 763, 279, 6574, 11, 7508, 362, 9731, 311, 6541, 279, 19065, 311, 7508, 426, 11, 5605, 430, 279, 2955, 374, 2288, 6485, 323, 430, 596, 3249, 279, 2082, 374, 3515, 12544, 31301, 10489, 382, 334, 13617, 6075, 25, 57277, 2028, 6671, 46480, 1268, 7508, 362, 2744, 86890, 7508, 426, 369, 872, 21294, 13, 18185, 1694, 8647, 369, 4477, 279, 2082, 11, 7508, 362, 84040, 82, 279, 19065, 311, 7508, 426, 11, 21039, 430, 279, 2955, 374, 279, 3789, 315, 279, 3575, 13, 1115, 7865, 539, 1193, 11705, 24408, 304, 279, 2128, 719, 1101, 305, 32551, 279, 3575, 99246, 1920, 11, 439, 7508, 426, 11321, 16399, 323, 46243, 311, 990, 3871, 311, 1505, 264, 6425, 13, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=Non