Output~2025-04-24 17:16:22.281361: [RequestOutput(request_id=1172, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Describe the differences between a pig and a cow. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 61885, 279, 12062, 1990, 264, 24623, 323, 264, 19923, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a response that describes the differences between a pig and a cow:\n\nPigs and cows are both domesticated mammals that are commonly raised for their meat, milk, and other products. However, they belong to different species and have several distinct differences. Here are some of the main differences between pigs and cows:\n\n**Physical Characteristics:**\n\n* Pigs are smaller than cows, with adults typically weighing between 50-300 kg (110-660 lbs), while cows can weigh up to 1,000 kg (2,200 lbs) or more.\n* Pigs have a more compact body shape, with a shorter neck and legs, whereas cows have a longer neck and legs.\n* Pigs have a thicker, smoother skin, while cows have a thicker, coarser coat of hair.\n* Pigs have a more rounded snout, while cows have a longer, more pointed snout.\n\n**Behavior:**\n\n* Pigs are social animals that live in groups, called sounders, while cows are also social but tend to live in smaller groups, called herds.\n* Pigs are more curious and playful, while cows are generally more docile and laid-back.\n* Pigs are known for their intelligence and problem-solving abilities, while cows are more instinctual and less intelligent.\n\n**Diet:**\n\n* Pigs are omnivores and will eat almost anything, including plants, grains, and insects, while cows are ruminants and primarily eat grasses, hay, and other plant-based foods.\n* Pigs are often raised on a diet of grains and other supplements, while cows are typically raised on a diet of grass and other forages.\n\n**Habitat:**\n\n* Pigs are often raised in pens or enclosures, while cows are typically raised on pasture or in fields.\n* Pigs are more adaptable to different environments and can thrive in a variety of climates, while cows are more sensitive to temperature and humidity and require specific conditions to thrive.\n\n**Products:**\n\n* Pigs are raised for their meat (pork), while cows are raised for their meat (beef) and milk (dairy products).\n* Pigs are also used for their skin, fat, and other by-products, while cows are used for their milk, hides, and other by-products.\n\nThese are just a few of the key differences between pigs and cows. While they share some similarities, they are distinct species with unique characteristics and uses.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 2077, 430, 16964, 279, 12062, 1990, 264, 24623, 323, 264, 19923, 1473, 47, 14801, 323, 46266, 527, 2225, 13018, 660, 56669, 430, 527, 17037, 9408, 369, 872, 13339, 11, 14403, 11, 323, 1023, 3956, 13, 4452, 11, 814, 9352, 311, 2204, 9606, 323, 617, 3892, 12742, 12062, 13, 5810, 527, 1063, 315, 279, 1925, 12062, 1990, 49910, 323, 46266, 1473, 334, 40353, 85084, 25, 57277, 9, 393, 14801, 527, 9333, 1109, 46266, 11, 449, 12884, 11383, 47826, 1990, 220, 1135, 12, 3101, 21647, 320, 5120, 12, 19274, 29160, 705, 1418, 46266, 649, 17988, 709, 311, 220, 16, 11, 931, 21647, 320, 17, 11, 1049, 29160, 8, 477, 810, 627, 9, 393, 14801, 617, 264, 810, 17251, 2547, 6211, 11, 449, 264, 24210, 13272, 323, 14535, 11, 20444, 46266, 617, 264, 5129, 13272, 323, 14535, 627, 9, 393, 14801, 617, 264, 59884, 11, 61405, 6930, 11, 1418, 46266, 617, 264, 59884, 11, 1080, 10642, 23724, 315, 7013, 627, 9, 393, 14801, 617, 26