Output~2025-04-24 17:18:19.602892: [RequestOutput(request_id=1230, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Find the lowest value for the following function ### Input: 6x^2 - 4x - 8 ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 7531, 279, 15821, 907, 369, 279, 2768, 734, 17010, 5688, 25, 220, 21, 87, 61, 17, 482, 220, 19, 87, 482, 220, 23, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='To find the lowest value of the function 6x^2 - 4x - 8, we need to complete the square.\n\nFirst, we can rewrite the function as:\n\n6x^2 - 4x - 8 = 6(x^2 - (2/3)x) - 8\n\nNext, we can add the square of half of the coefficient of the x term (which is 2/3) to both sides of the equation:\n\n6(x^2 - (2/3)x + (1/9)) - 8 + (4/3)^2\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n6(x - 1/3)^2 - 8 + 8/3\n\nThe lowest value of this function will occur when x - 1/3 = 0, which means x = 1/3. Plugging this value back into the original function, we get:\n\n6(1/3)^2 - 4(1/3) - 8 = 2/3 - 4/3 - 8 = -10/3\n\nSo, the lowest value of the function 6x^2 - 4x - 8 is -10/3.', token_ids=[1271, 1505, 279, 15821, 907, 315, 279, 734, 220, 21, 87, 61, 17, 482, 220, 19, 87, 482, 220, 23, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 4686, 279, 9518, 382, 5451, 11, 584, 649, 18622, 279, 734, 439, 1473, 21, 87, 61, 17, 482, 220, 19, 87, 482, 220, 23, 284, 220, 21, 2120, 61, 17, 482, 320, 17, 14, 18, 51824, 8, 482, 220, 23, 271, 5971, 11, 584, 649, 923, 279, 9518, 315, 4376,