 work options to attract a more diverse pool of candidates.\n5. Partner with diversity-focused organizations and universities to attract underrepresented groups.\n\n**III. Employee Development and Retention**\n\n1. Develop training programs that address unconscious bias, cultural competence, and inclusive communication.\n2. Offer mentorship and sponsorship programs to support underrepresented groups.\n3. Provide opportunities for professional development and career advancement.\n4. Foster a culture of inclusion by recognizing and rewarding diverse perspectives and contributions.\n5. Conduct regular employee engagement surveys to measure diversity and inclusion efforts.\n\n**IV. Inclusive Workplace Culture**\n\n1. Develop a comprehensive diversity and inclusion policy that outlines the company's commitment to diversity and inclusion.\n2. Establish a zero-tolerance policy for discrimination and harassment.\n3. Provide resources and support for employees with disabilities, including accommodations and accessibility features.\n4. Celebrate diversity through cultural events, observances, and employee resource groups.\n5. Encourage open communication and feedback through regular town hall meetings and anonymous feedback mechanisms.\n\n**V. Monitoring and Evaluation**\n\n1. Establish key performance indicators (KPIs) to measure diversity and inclusion progress.\n2. Conduct regular diversity and inclusion audits to identify areas for improvement.\n3. Analyze employee data to identify trends and patterns in diversity and inclusion.\n4. Share diversity and inclusion metrics with employees and stakeholders to promote transparency and accountability.\n5. Adjust the plan as needed based on data-driven insights and feedback.\n\n**VI. Leadership Accountability**\n\n1. Ensure senior leadership is committed to diversity and", token_ids=[334, 35, 1986, 7922, 279, 5664, 9009, 25, 362, 67963, 9878, 369, 13346, 57277, 1271, 7946, 21797, 1463, 1202, 32027, 11, 264, 2883, 2011, 11142, 264