d developmental delays in children.\n6. **Reduced lung function**: Long-term exposure to air pollution can lead to permanent damage to the lungs, reducing lung function and increasing the risk of respiratory problems.\n7. **Increased risk of premature death**: Exposure to air pollution has been linked to an increased risk of premature death, with estimates suggesting that air pollution is responsible for millions of premature deaths worldwide each year.\n8. **Increased risk of respiratory infections**: Long-term exposure to air pollution can weaken the immune system, making individuals more susceptible to respiratory infections such as pneumonia and bronchitis.\n9. **Eye, nose, and throat irritation**: Exposure to air pollution can cause eye, nose, and throat irritation, as well as headaches and fatigue.\n10. **Reduced quality of life**: Long-term exposure to air pollution can reduce an individual's quality of life, making it difficult to engage in physical activity, enjoy outdoor activities, and participate in daily life.\n\nIt is essential to take steps to reduce exposure to air pollution, such as using air purifiers, avoiding areas with high levels of pollution, and supporting policies that promote clean air.", token_ids=[6720, 9860, 14675, 311, 3805, 25793, 706, 1027, 10815, 311, 264, 7029, 2134, 315, 6129, 2890, 6372, 11, 2737, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 1079, 5682, 5382, 5435, 96618, 73782, 14675, 311, 8009, 3805, 4367, 649, 52875, 349, 4787, 1778, 439, 51643, 11, 21249, 54292, 535, 70524, 8624, 320, 34, 3143, 35, 705, 323, 31071, 331, 20000, 11, 6522, 311, 7319, 13803, 323, 11293, 21271, 734, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 5889, 822, 33945, 8624, 96618, 71866, 311, 3805, 25793, 706, 1027, 10815, 311, 459, 7319, 5326, 315, 4851, 8951, 11, 53572, 11, 323, 1023, 41713, 4455, 11, 902, 649, 3063, 311, 42227, 4648, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 34, 11967, 96618, 5843, 9860, 14675, 311, 3805, 25793, 706, 1027, 21771, 439, 264, 52788, 11968, 555, 279, 7327, 16784, 369, 8483, 389, 26211, 320, 40, 