Output~2025-04-24 17:22:08.790636: [RequestOutput(request_id=1324, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Create an analogy to explain cloud computing. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4324, 459, 56203, 311, 10552, 9624, 25213, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here\'s an analogy to explain cloud computing:\n\n"Imagine you have a large library with millions of books, but instead of storing them on your personal bookshelves, you store them in a massive, shared library building that\'s accessible to everyone in the city. This library is equipped with an infinite number of bookshelves, and each bookshelf can hold thousands of books.\n\nJust like how you can access any book you need from the library, cloud computing allows you to access and use computer resources, such as storage, processing power, and applications, from anywhere in the world, at any time. You don\'t need to own or maintain the physical infrastructure, just like you don\'t need to own the bookshelves or the books themselves.\n\nWhen you need to use a particular resource, you simply \'check it out\' from the cloud, just like you would check out a book from the library. You can use it for as long as you need it, and then return it when you\'re done. The cloud provider takes care of maintaining the infrastructure, updating the resources, and ensuring that everything runs smoothly.\n\nJust as the library has multiple copies of popular books to ensure that everyone can access them, cloud providers often have multiple servers and data centers to ensure that your data is always available and secure. And just as you can access the library from anywhere, cloud computing allows you to access your data and applications from any device with an internet connection, making it a powerful tool for collaboration, productivity, and innovation."', token_ids=[8586, 596, 459, 56203, 311, 10552, 9624, 25213, 1473, 1, 52157, 499, 617, 264, 3544, 6875, 449, 11990, 315, 6603, 11, 719, 4619, 315, 28672, 1124, 389, 701, 4443, 2363, 939, 4372, 11, 499, 3637, 1124, 304, 264, 11191, 11, 6222, 6875, 4857, 430, 596, 15987, 311, 5127, 304, 279, 3363, 13, 1115, 6875, 374, 19167, 449, 459, 24746, 1396, 315, 2363, 939, 4372, 11, 323, 1855, 2363, 55050, 649, 3412, 9214, 315, 6603, 382, 10156, 1093, 1268, 499, 649, 2680, 904, 2363, 499, 1205, 505, 279, 6875, 11, 9624, 25213, 6276, 499, 311, 2680, 323, 1005, 6500, 5070, 11, 1778, 439, 5942, 11, 8863, 2410, 11, 323, 8522, 11, 505, 12660, 304, 279, 1917, 11, 520, 904, 892, 13, 1472, 1541, 956, 1205, 311, 1866, 477, 10519, 279, 7106, 14054, 11, 1120, 1093, 499, 1541, 956, 1205, 311, 1866, 279, 2363, 939, 4372, 477, 279, 6603, 5694, 382, 4599, 499, 1205, 311, 1005, 264, 4040, 5211, 11, 499, 5042, 364, 2071, 433, 704, 6, 505, 279, 9624, 11, 1120, 1093, 499, 1053, 1817, 704, 264, 2363, 505, 279, 6875, 13, 1472, 649, 1005, 433, 369, 439, 1317, 439, 499, 1205, 433, 11, 323, 1243, 471, 433, 994, 499, 2351, 2884, 13, 578, 9624, 9287, 5097, 2512, 315, 20958, 279, 14054, 11, 21686, 279, 5070, 11, 323, 23391, 430, 4395, 8640, 39511, 382, 10156, 439, 279, 6875, 706, 5361, 11236, 315, 5526, 6603, 311, 6106, 430, 5127, 649, 2680, 1124, 11, 9624, 12850, 3629, 617, 5361, 16692, 323, 828, 19169, 311, 6106, 430, 701, 828, 374, 2744, 2561, 323, 9966, 13, 1628, 1120, 439, 499, 649, 2680, 279, 6875, 505, 12660, 11, 9624, 25213, 6276, 499, 311, 2680, 701, 828, 323, 8522, 505, 904, 3756, 449, 459, 7757, 3717, 11, 3339, 433, 264, 8147, 5507, 369, 20632, 11, 