ves in Confederate territory.\n* May 1-4: The Siege of Vicksburg is lifted, giving the Union control of the Mississippi River.\n* July 1-3: The Battle of Gettysburg is fought in Pennsylvania, resulting in a Union victory.\n* July 4: The Battle of Vicksburg is fought in Mississippi, resulting in a Union victory.\n* November 19: The Gettysburg Address is delivered by President Lincoln.\n\n**1864**\n\n* May 4-28: The Battle of the Wilderness is fought in Virginia, resulting in a stalemate.\n* May 8-21: The Battle of Spotsylvania Courthouse is fought in Virginia, resulting in a stalemate.\n* June 15-18: The Battle of Petersburg is fought in Virginia, resulting in a stalemate.\n* July 30: The Battle of the Crater is fought in Virginia, resulting in a Confederate victory.\n* August 5: The Siege of Atlanta begins, resulting in the capture of the city on September 2.\n* November 8: Abraham Lincoln is re-elected as President.\n\n**1865**\n\n* January 31: The', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 25845, 315, 279, 3778, 16803, 5111, 1473, 334, 9714, 16, 57277, 9, 5936, 220, 717, 25, 578, 3778, 16803, 5111, 12302, 994, 57457, 8603, 4027, 389, 9323, 17312, 520, 11246, 8279, 466, 304, 53393, 40282, 11, 4987, 13030, 627, 9, 5936, 220, 868, 25, 4900, 37488, 25379, 6880, 369, 220, 2075, 11, 931, 23872, 311, 28321, 279, 53848, 627, 9, 3297, 220, 508, 25, 13286, 513, 26785, 505, 279, 9323, 11, 8272, 555, 32790, 11, 24097, 11, 323, 4892, 13030, 627, 9, 5651, 220, 23, 25, 578, 9323, 19574, 41255, 279, 2700, 3363, 315, 473, 1683, 300, 763, 1169, 11, 4892, 13030, 627, 9, 5887, 220, 1691, 25, 578, 5629, 16506, 315, 22353, 6588, 374, 21095, 3221, 2418, 395, 300, 11, 13286, 11, 13239, 304, 264, 57457, 12845, 382, 334, 9714, 17, 57277, 9, 6186, 220, 16, 25, 578, 5867, 1149, 49686, 1322, 34084, 374, 11136, 555, 4900, 25379, 11, 67817, 682, 32760, 304, 57457, 18455, 627, 9, 5936, 220, 21, 12, 22, 25, 578, 16506, 315, 1443, 321, 2319, 374, 21095, 304, 18561, 24097, 11, 13239, 304, 264, 9323, 12845, 627, 