Output~2025-04-24 17:22:33.962237: [RequestOutput(request_id=1329, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Explain the basic principles of the theory of evolution. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 83017, 279, 6913, 16565, 315, 279, 10334, 315, 15740, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='The theory of evolution is a fundamental concept in biology that explains how species change over time through the process of natural selection, genetic drift, mutation, and gene flow. The basic principles of the theory of evolution can be summarized as follows:\n\n1. **Descent with Modification**: All living organisms share a common ancestor and have evolved over time through the process of modification. This means that all species have a shared history and have changed over time through the accumulation of genetic changes.\n2. **Variation**: All individuals within a species exhibit genetic variation, which is the raw material for evolution. This variation can arise through mutation, genetic recombination, and gene flow.\n3. **Heritability**: The characteristics of an individual are determined by their genetic makeup, which is passed on from one generation to the next. This means that the traits of an individual are inherited from their parents.\n4. **Adaptation**: As the environment changes, individuals with traits that are better suited to the new environment are more likely to survive and reproduce, passing on their advantageous traits to their offspring. This is the process of natural selection.\n5. **Natural Selection**: The process of natural selection acts on the variation present in a population, favoring individuals with traits that are better adapted to their environment. This leads to the accumulation of adaptations over time.\n6. **Speciation**: Over time, the accumulation of adaptations can lead to the formation of new species. This occurs when a population becomes reproductively isolated from other populations and evolves distinct characteristics that are not shared with other species.\n7. **Gradualism**: Evolution is a gradual process that occurs over long periods of time. It is not a sudden or rapid process, but rather a slow and continuous process of change.\n8. **Fossil Record**: The fossil record provides evidence for the gradual changes that have occurred over time, as well as the transitional forms that have given rise to new species.\n9. **Comparative Anatomy and Embryology**: The study of comparative anatomy and embryology reveals the similarities and homologies between different species, providing evidence for their common ancestry.\n10. **Molecular Biology**: The study of molecular biology has confirmed the relatedness of different species and provided further evidence for evolution through the analysis of DNA and protein sequences.\n\nIn summary, the theory of evolution is based on the principles of descent with modification, variation, heritability, adaptation, natural selection, speciation, gradualism, the fossil record, comparative anatomy and embryology, and molecular biology. These principles provide a', token_ids=[791, 10334, 315, 15740, 374, 264, 16188, 7434, 304, 34458, 430, 15100, 1268, 9606, 2349, 927, 892, 1555, 279, 1920, 315, 5933, 6727, 11, 19465, 34738, 11, 27472, 11, 323, 15207, 6530, 13, 578, 6913, 16565, 315, 279, 10334, 315, 15740, 649, 387, 69729, 439, 11263, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 5001, 1189, 449, 74955, 96618, 2052, 5496, 44304, 4430, 264, 4279, 46831, 323, 617, 28995, 927, 892, 1555, 279, 1920, 315, 17466, 13, 1115, 3445, 430, 682, 9606, 617, 264, 6222, 3925, 323, 617, 5614, 927, 892, 1555, 279, 46835, 315, 19465, 4442, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 57235, 367, 96618, 2052, 7931, 2949, 264, 9606, 31324, 19465, 23851, 11, 902, 374, 279, 7257, 3769, 369, 15740, 13, 1115, 23851, 649, 31889, 1555, 27472, 11, 19465, 312, 76128, 11, 323, 15207, 6530, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 21364, 275, 2968, 96618, 578, 17910, 315, 459, 3927, 527, 11075, 555, 872, 19465, 27649, 11, 902, 374, 5946, 389, 505, 832, 9659, 311, 279, 1828, 13, 1115, 3445, 430, 279, 25022, 315, 459, 3927, 527, 28088, 505, 872, 6699, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 2654, 2756, 367, 96618, 1666, 279, 4676, 4442, 11, 7931, 449, 25022, 430, 527, 2731, 32599, 311, 279, 502, 4676, 527, 810, 4461, 311, 18167, 323, 23645, 11, 12579, 389, 872, 76824, 25022, 311, 872, 46471, 13, 1115, 374, 279, 1920, 315, 5933, 6727, 627, 20, 13, 3146, 55381, 25117, 96618, 578, 1920, 315, 5933, 6727, 14385, 389, 279, 23851, 3118, 304, 264, 7187, 11, 4799, 287, 7931, 449, 25022, 430, 527, 2731, 30464, 311, 872, 4676, 13, 1115, 11767, 311, 279, 46835, 315, 77765, 927, 892, 627, 21, 13, 3146, 8491, 7246, 96618, 6193, 892, 11, 279, 46835, 315, 77765, 649, 3063, 311, 279, 18488, 315, 502, 9606, 13, 1115, 13980, 994, 264, 7187, 9221, 312, 3107, 3210, 25181, 505, 1023, 22673, 323, 93054, 12742, 17910, 430, 527, 539, 6222, 449, 1023, 9606, 627, 22, 13, 3146, 24956, 940, 2191, 96618, 38321, 374, 264, 53722, 1920, 430, 13980, 927, 1317, 18852, 315, 892, 13, 1102, 374, 539, 264, 11210, 477, 11295, 1920, 11, 719, 4856, 264, 6435, 323, 19815, 1920, 315, 2349, 627, 23, 13, 3146, 37, 85061, 13896, 96618, 578, 31376, 3335, 5825, 6029, 369, 279, 53722, 4442, 430, 617, 10222, 927, 892, 11, 439, 1664, 439, 279, 66743, 7739, 430, 617, 2728, 10205, 311, 502, 9606, 627, 24, 13, 3146, 17561, 1413, 80282, 323, 30227, 894, 2508, 96618, 578, 4007, 315, 55394, 62690, 323, 44481, 2508, 21667, 279, 43874, 323, 5105, 9268, 1990, 2204, 9606, 11, 8405, 6029, 369, 872, 4279, 6