Output~2025-04-24 17:24:31.254807: [RequestOutput(request_id=1370, prompt='<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{"Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Please provide a brief plot summary of the novel \'To Kill a Mockingbird\' by Harper Lee. ### Response:"}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n', prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 5018, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 5321, 3493, 264, 10015, 7234, 12399, 315, 279, 11775, 364, 1271, 27933, 264, 14905, 287, 23414, 6, 555, 33107, 12336, 13, 17010, 6075, 3047, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a brief plot summary of the novel "To Kill a Mockingbird" by Harper Lee:\n\nSet in the Deep South during the 1930s, "To Kill a Mockingbird" is a classic novel that explores issues of racial injustice, tolerance, and the loss of innocence. The story is told through the eyes of Scout Finch, a young girl who lives with her older brother Jem and their father, Atticus, in the fictional town of Maycomb, Alabama.\n\nThe story centers around the trial of Tom Robinson, a black man who is falsely accused of raping a white woman, Mayella Ewell. Atticus, a lawyer who is known for his fairness and integrity, agrees to defend Tom despite knowing he\'ll face prejudice and hostility from the community. As the trial approaches, Scout and Jem learn about the injustices faced by African Americans in their community and the deep-seated racial tensions that exist.\n\nThroughout the trial, Atticus delivers a powerful defense of Tom, highlighting the inconsistencies in the prosecution\'s case and the lack of evidence against Tom. However, despite his efforts, the jury delivers a guilty verdict, which is met with widespread approval from the white community.\n\nThe novel takes a dramatic turn when Bob Ewell, Mayella\'s father and the man who accused Tom, attempts to attack Scout and Jem one night. However, Boo Radley, a reclusive neighbor who has been the subject of local legend and rumors, intervenes and saves the children. In the process, Bob Ewell is killed, and Boo is injured.\n\nAs the story concludes, Scout and her father reflect on the events of the trial and the loss of innocence that has occurred. Atticus\'s defense of Tom has taught Scout and Jem valuable lessons about empathy, compassion, and the importance of doing what is right in the face of overwhelming opposition. The novel ends with Scout realizing that Boo Radley, who has become a symbol of kindness and redemption, has been watching over her and her brother throughout the story, and that he is not the monster she had imagined him to be.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 10015, 7234, 12399, 315, 279, 11775, 330, 1271, 27933, 264, 14905, 287, 23414, 1, 555, 33107, 12336, 1473, 1681, 304, 279, 18682, 4987, 2391, 279, 220, 7285, 15, 82, 11, 330, 1271, 27933, 264, 14905, 287, 23414, 1, 374, 264, 11670, 11775, 430, 41424, 4819, 315, 19739, 51215, 11, 25065, 11, 323, 279, 4814, 315, 57311, 13, 578, 3446, 374, 3309, 1555, 279, 6548, 315, 48635, 96333, 11, 264, 3995, 3828, 889, 6439, 449, 1077, 9191, 10868, 622, 336, 323, 872, 7126, 11, 7867, 59344, 11, 304, 279, 44682, 6424, 315, 3297, 22631, 11, 21272, 382, 791, 3446, 19169, 2212, 279, 9269, 315, 8529, 28280, 11, 264, 3776, 893, 889, 374, 61456, 13487, 315, 87546, 264, 4251, 5333, 11, 3297, 6985, 469, 9336, 13, 7867, 59344, 11, 264, 15779, 889, 374, 3967, 369, 813, 51841, 323, 17025, 11, 34008, 311, 10726, 8529, 8994, 14392, 568, 3358, 3663, 48786, 323, 61029, 505, 279, 4029, 13, 1666, 279, 9269, 20414, 11, 48635, 323, 622, 336, 4048, 922, 279, 98753, 1238, 17011, 555, 11904, 9053, 304, 872, 4029, 323, 279, 5655, 7962, 660, 19739, 39510, 430, 3