ing sight. According to local legend, the causeway was built by a giant to reach Scotland and fight a rival giant, adding a touch of myth and magic to this already impressive natural formation.", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 2380, 1355, 18886, 12399, 315, 279, 1495, 1473, 791, 41841, 596, 45446, 3195, 374, 264, 5933, 5895, 7559, 304, 1556, 10893, 11, 17355, 14990, 11, 31706, 315, 13489, 220, 1272, 11, 931, 311, 220, 1135, 11, 931, 958, 90582, 3122, 3223, 8310, 13, 4314, 11191, 8310, 10205, 505, 279, 9581, 323, 14841, 220, 18, 8931, 311, 279, 44106, 1948, 11, 6968, 264, 5016, 323, 57192, 14254, 13, 10771, 311, 2254, 13314, 11, 279, 5353, 3195, 574, 5918, 555, 264, 14880, 311, 5662, 19627, 323, 4465, 264, 21425, 14880, 11, 7999, 264, 5916, 315, 21849, 323, 11204, 311, 420, 2736, 16358, 5933, 18488, 13, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None)], finished=True, metrics=None, lora_request=None, num_cached_tokens=None, multi_modal_placeholders={})]
