Output~2025-04-24 17:29:10.318981: [RequestOutput(request_id=1500, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write a description for a barbecue recipe. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 264, 4096, 369, 264, 62312, 11363, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="**Summer's Sweetest BBQ Ribs Recipe**\n\nGet ready to fire up the grill and indulge in the most tender, fall-off-the-bone ribs of your life! This mouthwatering BBQ recipe is a classic summer staple that's sure to become a family favorite.\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n* 2 racks of pork ribs (about 4 pounds total)\n* 1 cup of your favorite BBQ sauce\n* 1/4 cup of brown sugar\n* 2 tablespoons of smoked paprika\n* 1 teaspoon of garlic powder\n* 1 teaspoon of onion powder\n* 1 teaspoon of salt\n* 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper\n* 1/4 cup of apple cider vinegar\n* 1/4 cup of water\n* 2 tablespoons of olive oil\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Preheat your grill to medium-low heat (275°F).\n2. In a small bowl, mix together the brown sugar, smoked paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, salt, and black pepper.\n3. Remove the membrane from the back of the ribs (this will help the rub penetrate the meat).\n4. Apply the dry rub evenly to both racks of ribs, making sure to coat all surfaces.\n5. Place the ribs on the grill, bone-side down. Close the lid and cook for 2 hours.\n6. After 2 hours, brush the ribs with the BBQ sauce and flip them over. Close the lid and cook for an additional 30 minutes.\n7. Remove the ribs from the grill and let them rest for 10 minutes before slicing and serving.\n\n**Tips and Variations:**\n\n* For an extra crispy crust, broil the ribs for an additional 2-3 minutes after cooking.\n* Try using different types of BBQ sauce, such as Kansas City-style or Carolina-style, for a unique flavor profile.\n* Add some wood chips to the grill for a smoky flavor.\n* Serve with your favorite sides, such as coleslaw, baked beans, or corn on the cob.\n\n**Get Ready for a Rib-Tickling Good Time!**\n\nThis BBQ recipe is sure to become a summer staple in your household. With its tender, fall-off-the-bone meat and sweet, tangy BBQ sauce, you'll be the envy of all your friends and family. So fire up the grill, grab a plate, and get ready to indulge in the most delicious ribs of your life!", token_ids=[334, 51787, 596, 27687, 478, 46377, 432, 55441, 26371, 57277, 1991, 5644, 311, 4027, 709, 279, 40158, 323, 68190, 304, 279, 1455, 28682, 11, 4498, 12744, 10826, 1481, 606, 56249, 315, 701, 2324, 0, 1115, 11013, 13284, 287, 46377, 11363, 374, 264, 11670, 7474, 50056, 430, 596, 2771, 311, 3719, 264, 3070, 7075, 382, 334, 46847, 25, 57277, 9, 220, 17, 66968, 315, 36167, 56249, 320, 9274, 220, 19, 16701, 2860, 340, 9, 220, 16, 10747, 315, 701, 7075, 46377, 19737, 198, 9, 220, 16, 14, 19, 10747, 315, 14198, 13465, 198, 9, 220, 17, 56588, 315, 48637, 26365, 41554, 198, 9, 220, 16, 42384, 315, 31735, 17138, 198, 9, 220, 16, 42384, 315, 38427, 17138, 198, 9, 220, 16, 42384, 315, 12290, 198, 9, 220, 16, 14, 17, 42384, 315, 3776, 25349, 198, 9, 220, 16, 14, 19, 10747, 315, 24149, 66155, 47205, 198, 9, 220, 16, 14, 19, 10747, 315, 3090, 198, 9, 220, 17, 56588, 315, 33213, 5707, 271, 334, 56391, 25, 57277, 16, 13, 5075, 20559, 701, 40158, 311, 11298, 60369, 8798, 320, 14417, 59572, 4390, 17, 13, 763, 264, 2678, 19763, 11, 6651, 3871, 279, 14198, 13465, 11, 48637, 26365, 41554, 11, 31735, 17138, 11, 38427, 17138, 11, 12290, 11, 323, 3776, 25349, 627, 18, 13, 11016, 279, 39654, 505, 279, 12