Output~2025-04-24 17:29:53.507822: [RequestOutput(request_id=1514, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Tell a story using the following words: ### Input: alien, amazement, disguise, library, purple ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 25672, 264, 3446, 1701, 279, 2768, 4339, 25, 17010, 5688, 25, 20167, 11, 1097, 1394, 1133, 11, 65081, 11, 6875, 11, 25977, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="As I walked into the old library, I couldn't help but feel a sense of amazement at the sheer volume of books that surrounded me. The musty smell of aged paper and leather-bound tomes filled my nostrils, and I felt like I had stepped into a different world. Suddenly, I heard a faint humming noise coming from the corner of the room. I turned to see a small, purple creature with large, round eyes peeking out from behind a shelf.\n\nIt was an alien, and it was wearing a ridiculous disguise - a pair of thick, black-rimmed glasses and a fedora. I couldn't help but laugh at the absurdity of it all. The alien looked up at me and smiled, and I could sense its amazement at the vast collection of books that surrounded us.\n\nThe alien, who introduced himself as Zorvath, explained that he was on a mission to collect the most rare and valuable books in the galaxy. He had heard that this library was the perfect place to find them, and he was determined to get his hands on as many as he could.\n\nI watched in amazement as Zorvath expertly navigated the shelves, his long, slender fingers dancing across the spines of the books as he searched for the perfect additions to his collection. As we browsed together, I learned that Zorvath was not only a bookworm, but also a master of disguise and deception. He could change his appearance at will, and had a talent for blending in with his surroundings.\n\nAs the hours passed, I found myself growing more and more fond of Zorvath's company. Despite his alien nature, he was kind and gentle, and his love of books was infectious. Together, we discovered hidden gems and rare treasures, and I learned that even the most unlikely of creatures could share a passion for the written word.\n\nAs the sun began to set, Zorvath bid me farewell, his purple skin glowing softly in the fading light. I watched as he disappeared into the night, his disguise and amazement leaving me with a sense of wonder that I would never forget.", token_ids=[2170, 358, 15203, 1139, 279, 2362, 6875, 11, 358, 7846, 956, 1520, 719, 2733, 264, 5647, 315, 1097, 1394, 1133, 520, 279, 33638, 8286, 315, 6603, 430, 23712, 757, 13, 578, 2011, 88, 22843, 315, 20330, 5684, 323, 18012, 50962, 311, 9004, 10409, 856, 57426, 8839, 11, 323, 358, 6612, 1093, 358, 1047, 25319, 1139, 264, 2204, 1917, 13, 58801, 11, 358, 6755, 264, 38678, 87427, 12248, 5108, 505, 279, 9309, 315, 279, 3130, 13, 358, 6656, 311, 1518, 264, 2678, 11, 25977, 17661, 449, 3544, 11, 4883, 6548, 33692, 287, 704, 505, 4920, 264, 28745, 382, 2181, 574, 459, 20167, 11, 323, 433, 574, 12512, 264, 27873, 65081, 482, 264, 6857, 315, 12314, 11, 3776, 3880, 318, 2106, 29247, 323, 264, 23114, 6347, 13, 358, 7846, 956, 1520, 719, 12835, 520, 279, 32677, 488, 315, 433, 682, 13, 578, 20167, 7111, 709, 520, 757, 323, 31645, 11, 323, 358, 1436, 5647, 1202, 1097, 1394, 1133, 520, 279, 13057, 4526, 315, 6603, 430, 23712, 603, 382, 791, 20167, 11, 889, 11784, 5678, 439, 1901, 269, 85, 589, 11, 11497, 