velope breakdown**: The nuclear envelope, which is the double membrane that surrounds the nucleus, breaks down.\n3. **Spindle fibers formation**: The spindle fibers, which are made up of microtubules, begin to form and attach to the centromeres of the chromosomes.\n4. **Chromosome separation**: The chromosomes begin to separate from each other and move to opposite poles of the cell.\n\n**Metaphase**\n\nDuring metaphase, the chromosomes line up at the center of the cell, attached to the spindle fibers. The following events occur during metaphase:\n\n1. **Chromosome alignment**: The chromosomes line up at the center of the cell, attached to the spindle fibers.\n2. **Chromosome separation**: The chromosomes are now fully separated and attached to the spindle fibers.\n\n**Anaphase**\n\nAnaphase is the stage during which the sister chromatids separate and move to opposite poles of the cell. The following events occur during anaphase:\n\n1. **Sister chromatid separation**: The sister chromatids separate and move to opposite poles of the cell.\n2. **Chromosome separation**: The chromosomes are now fully separated and attached to the spindle fibers.\n\n**Telophase**\n\nTelophase is the final stage of mitosis, during which the nuclear', token_ids=[55470, 10934, 374, 279, 1920, 315, 2849, 13096, 430, 3135, 304, 1403, 10003, 7917, 430, 527, 52033, 20086, 311, 279, 2748, 2849, 13, 1102, 374, 264, 16996, 1920, 304, 279, 2324, 11008, 315, 384, 3178, 661, 14546, 7917, 11, 2737, 10099, 11, 11012, 11, 323, 81540, 13, 578, 1920, 315, 5568, 10934, 374, 6485, 323, 18065, 3892, 18094, 11, 902, 527, 7633, 3770, 1473, 334, 3386, 26199, 57277, 791, 1920, 315, 5568, 10934, 12302, 449, 958, 26199, 11, 902, 374, 279, 22807, 6566, 315, 279, 2849, 11008, 13, 12220, 958, 26199, 11, 279, 2849, 28815, 11, 29641, 988, 1202, 15922, 11, 323, 48542, 369, 2849, 13096, 13, 578, 2768, 4455, 12446, 2391, 958, 26199, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 38, 16, 10474, 96618, 578, 2849, 28815, 323, 48542, 369, 15922, 48891,