Output~2025-04-24 17:31:26.500829: [RequestOutput(request_id=1548, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Find the exact value of this trigonometric expression. ### Input: cos(π/3) ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 7531, 279, 4839, 907, 315, 420, 54033, 263, 24264, 7645, 13, 17010, 5688, 25, 8119, 7, 49345, 14, 18, 8, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='To find the exact value of the trigonometric expression cos(π/3), we can use the fact that cos(π/3) is equal to the adjacent side over the hypotenuse in a 30-60-90 triangle.\n\nIn a 30-60-90 triangle, the ratio of the sides is 1:√3:2. This means that the adjacent side (which is opposite the 30-degree angle) is 1 unit long, and the hypotenuse is 2 units long.\n\nUsing this information, we can find the value of cos(π/3) as follows:\n\ncos(π/3) = adjacent side / hypotenuse\n= 1 / 2\n= 0.5\n\nTherefore, the exact value of the trigonometric expression cos(π/3) is 0.5.', token_ids=[1271, 1505, 279, 4839, 907, 315, 279, 54033, 263, 24264, 7645, 8119, 7, 49345, 14, 18, 705, 584, 649, 1005, 279, 2144, 430, 8119, 7, 49345, 14, 18, 8, 374, 6273, 311, 279, 24894, 3185, 927, 279, 9950, 66728, 817, 304, 264, 220, 966, 12, 1399, 12, 1954, 22217, 382, 644, 264, 220, 966, 12, 1399, 12, 1954, 22217, 11, 279, 11595, 315, 279, 11314, 374, 220, 16, 25, 110682, 18, 25, 17, 13, 1115, 3445, 430, 279, 24894, 3185, 320, 8370, 374