get:\n\n`(x + 2)(x - 1) = 0`\n\nThis gives us two possible values for `x`: `x = -2` or `x = 1`.\n\nSince `x` is the value of the expression inside the radical, it must be non-negative. Therefore, `x = 1`.\n\nNow that we have the value of `x`, we can substitute it back into the expression:\n\n`sqrt(2 - sqrt(2 - sqrt(2 - sqrt(2 - ...)))` = `sqrt(2 - 1)` = `sqrt(1)` = `1`\n\nSo, the", token_ids=[32, 11670, 3187, 315, 264, 24997, 18336, 7645, 2268, 1271, 15806, 420, 7645, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 1833, 279, 2015, 315, 7677, 320, 1777, 6204, 1950, 7887, 16, 13, 55215, 279, 9358, 3646, 18336, 1176, 25, 1595, 27986, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 2564, 595, 63, 284, 1595, 27986, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 2564, 7861, 4077, 17, 13, 30658, 279, 9358, 3646, 18336, 449, 1202, 907, 25, 1595, 27986, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 2564, 7861, 63, 284, 1595, 27986, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 865, 595, 7964, 1405, 1595, 87, 63, 374, 279, 907, 315, 279, 7645, 4871, 279, 9358, 3646, 18336, 627, 18, 13, 55215, 279, 1828, 9358, 18336, 25, 1595, 27986, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 865, 595, 63, 284, 1595, 27986, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 865, 595, 4077, 19, 13, 30658, 279, 1828, 9358, 18336, 449, 1202, 907, 25, 1595, 27986, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 865, 595, 63, 284, 1595, 27986, 7, 17, 482, 865, 50337, 20, 13, 45901, 7504, 220, 17, 12, 19, 3156, 279, 7645, 15858, 9803, 311, 264, 3254, 907, 382, 10267, 596, 656, 430, 1473, 63, 27986, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 2564, 7861, 63, 284, 1595, 27986, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 865, 595, 63, 284, 1595, 27986, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 865, 7861, 63, 284, 1595, 27986, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 865, 7861, 63, 284, 1595, 27986, 7, 17, 482, 18430, 7, 17, 482, 865, 595, 63, 284, 1595, 27986, 7, 17, 482, 865, 8, 19884, 7184, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 1505, 279, 907, 315, 1595, 87, 29687, 2057