rain to Washington D.C. (approximately 4 hours)\n* Visit the National Mall, including the Lincoln Memorial, World War II Memorial, and the Reflecting Pool\n* Explore the Smithsonian National Air and Space Museum or the National Museum of Natural History\n* Enjoy dinner at Ben's Chili Bowl, a D.C. institution\n\n**Day 4: Washington D.C.**\n\n* Visit the United States Capitol Building and the Supreme Court\n* Explore the National Archives, home to the Declaration of Independence, the Constitution, and the Bill of Rights\n* Take a stroll through the beautiful Kenilworth Aquatic Gardens or the National Arboretum\n* Enjoy dinner at Old Ebbitt Grill, a historic restaurant near the White House\n\n**Day 5: Philadelphia**\n\n* Take a morning train to Philadelphia (approximately 2 hours)\n* Visit Independence Hall, where the Declaration of Independence and the Constitution were signed\n* Explore the Liberty Bell Center and take a stroll through Independence National Historical Park\n* Enjoy a classic Philly cheesesteak at Pat's King of Steaks or Geno's Steaks\n\n**Day 6: Boston**\n\n* Take a morning train to Boston (approximately 4.5 hours)\n* Visit the Freedom Trail, a 2.5-mile historic walking trail that takes you through 16 iconic sites, including the Old State House, Faneuil Hall, and the USS Constitution\n* Explore the Boston Common and the Public Garden, home to the famous Swan Boats\n* Enjoy dinner at Neptune Oyster, a historic seafood restaurant", token_ids=[29815, 389, 279, 7754, 323, 1988, 11, 358, 4265, 387, 6380, 311, 1520, 3197, 264, 220, 22, 11477, 8577, 311, 279, 7427, 13, 5810, 596, 264, 12090, 74004, 1473, 334, 10369, 220, 16, 25, 93198, 304, 1561, 4356, 4409, 57277, 9, 18925, 535, 520, 3842, 435, 13, 24573, 7327, 21348, 320, 41, 28096, 8, 304, 279, 6693, 198, 9, 4343, 3502, 311, 701, 9689, 304, 14013, 28931, 29890, 323, 7878, 268, 709, 198, 9, 78137, 279, 13658, 24919, 279, 27373, 8691, 15992, 11, 10913, 5657, 11, 323, 279, 21080, 3314, 17283, 198, 9, 23485,