Output~2025-04-24 17:37:35.891350: [RequestOutput(request_id=1668, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write an anecdote about the power of optimism. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 459, 50750, 1295, 922, 279, 2410, 315, 54508, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='I\'d be happy to share an anecdote about the power of optimism!\n\nI\'ll never forget the story of my grandmother, who was diagnosed with stage 3 breast cancer when she was just 55 years old. The news was devastating, and my family was heartbroken. But my grandmother, being the optimist that she was, refused to let the diagnosis define her. Instead, she chose to focus on the positive and the possibilities.\n\nShe started attending therapy sessions, where she learned to reframe her thoughts and focus on the present moment. She began to see the beauty in the little things, like the sunshine, the birds singing, and the love of her family. She started to prioritize self-care, taking long walks, practicing yoga, and cooking healthy meals.\n\nAs she went through her treatment, my grandmother\'s optimism was contagious. She inspired her family and friends to adopt a similar mindset, and soon our entire household was filled with positivity and hope. We would have family gatherings, where we would share stories of our own struggles and triumphs, and my grandmother would remind us that every cloud has a silver lining.\n\nOne day, during a particularly tough time in her treatment, my grandmother received some devastating news - the cancer had spread to her bones. But instead of giving up, she chose to focus on the progress she had made so far and the fact that she was still alive. She told us, "I may not have control over my health, but I can control how I respond to it. I choose to be optimistic and grateful for every day I have."\n\nHer words were like a balm to our souls. We rallied around her, and together, we faced the challenges ahead with renewed hope and determination. And you know what? My grandmother not only beat the odds, but she also inspired countless others to do the same. Her story is a testament to the power of optimism, and I will always cherish the lessons she taught me about the importance of staying positive, even in the darkest of times.', token_ids=[40, 4265, 387, 6380, 311, 4430, 459, 50750, 1295, 922, 279, 2410, 315, 54508, 2268, 40, 3358, 2646, 10894, 279, 3446, 315, 856, 39284, 11, 889, 574, 29704, 449, 6566, 220, 18, 17659, 9572, 994, 1364, 574, 1120, 220, 2131, 1667, 2362, 13, 578, 3754, 574, 33318, 11, 323, 856, 3070, 574, 4851, 50009, 13, 2030, 856, 39284, 11, 1694, 279, 7706, 380, 430, 1364, 574, 11, 16436, 311, 1095, 279, 23842, 7124, 1077, 13, 12361, 11, 1364, 14896, 311, 5357, 389, 279, 6928, 323, 279, 24525, 382, 8100, 3940, 24096, 15419, 16079, 11, 1405, 1364, 9687, 311, 312, 6906, 1077, 11555, 323, 5357, 389, 279, 3118, 4545, 13, 3005, 6137, 311, 1518, 279, 13444, 304, 279, 2697, 2574, 11, 1093, 279, 52495, 11, 279, 20229, 26139, 11, 323, 279, 3021, 315, 1077, 3070, 13, 3005, 3940, 311, 63652, 659, 41206, 11, 4737, 1317, 23291, 11, 36666, 27102, 11, 323, 17677, 9498, 21644, 382, 2170, 1364, 4024, 1555, 1077, 6514, 11, 856, 39284, 596, 54508, 574, 89534, 13, 3005, 14948, 1077, 3070, 323, 4885, 311, 11142, 264, 4528, 40543, 11, 323, 5246, 1057, 4553, 14048, 574, 10409, 449, 98042, 323, 3987, 13, 1226, 1053, 617, 3070, 66237, 11, 1405, 584, 1053, 4430, 7493, 315, 1057, 1866, 28970, 323, 38586, 82, 11, 323, 856, 39284