Output~2025-04-24 17:37:53.786023: [RequestOutput(request_id=1672, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write a poem about the beauty of the night sky. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 264, 33894, 922, 279, 13444, 315, 279, 3814, 13180, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is a poem about the beauty of the night sky:\n\nThe night sky, a canvas so divine,\nA tapestry of twinkling stars, a celestial shrine.\nThe moon, a glowing orb of silver light,\nCasts shadows dark, on the world below tonight.\n\nThe stars, like diamonds, scattered across the sky,\nA million points of light, that catch the eye.\nTheir gentle twinkle, a lullaby to the soul,\nA reminder of the magic, that makes us whole.\n\nThe constellations, a map of ancient lore,\nA guide to the gods, and the secrets they store.\nAndromeda's spiral arms, a whirlpool of blue,\nA reminder of the mysteries, that await us anew.\n\nThe night sky, a reflection of our own design,\nA mirror to the soul, where dreams and hopes entwine.\nA place where we can escape, from the world's loud din,\nAnd find our place, among the stars within.\n\nSo let us gaze upon, this celestial show,\nAnd let our spirits soar, as the stars begin to glow.\nFor in the beauty of the night sky, we find our peace,\nAnd a sense of wonder, that the world can't release.", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 33894, 922, 279, 13444, 315, 279, 3814, 13180, 1473, 791, 3814, 13180, 11, 264, 10247, 779, 30467, 345, 32, 17401, 4720, 315,