Output~2025-04-24 17:41:23.061114: [RequestOutput(request_id=1744, prompt='<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{\'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Define the term "cognitive dissonance". ### Response:\'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n', prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 19127, 279, 4751, 330, 66, 51549, 834, 942, 685, 3343, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Cognitive dissonance is a psychological phenomenon that occurs when an individual holds two or more beliefs, values, or attitudes that are inconsistent with each other, causing a feeling of discomfort, tension, or anxiety. This discomfort is often referred to as "dissonance." The theory of cognitive dissonance was first proposed by psychologist Leon Festinger in 1957 and suggests that people have a fundamental motivation to reduce this dissonance and achieve cognitive consistency.\n\nWhen an individual is confronted with information that contradicts their existing beliefs or attitudes, they may experience cognitive dissonance. For example, if someone believes that smoking is harmless, but then learns that smoking can cause serious health problems, they may feel a sense of dissonance. To reduce this dissonance, the individual may change their beliefs or attitudes to align with the new information, or they may rationalize or justify their existing beliefs to avoid the discomfort.\n\nCognitive dissonance can also occur when an individual\'s behavior is inconsistent with their attitudes or values. For instance, if someone claims to value honesty but is caught lying, they may experience dissonance. To reduce this dissonance, they may try to justify their behavior or change their attitudes to align with their actions.\n\nOverall, cognitive dissonance is a powerful psychological force that can drive individuals to change their beliefs, attitudes, and behaviors to achieve a sense of consistency and reduce the discomfort associated with holding conflicting ideas.', token_ids=[34, 51549, 834, 942, 685, 374, 264, 24064, 25885, 430, 13980, 994, 459, 3927, 10187, 1403, 477, 810, 21463, 11, 2819, 11, 477, 33726, 430, 527, 40240, 449, 1855, 1023, 11, 14718, 264, 8430, 315, 44776, 11, 24408, 11, 477, 18547, 13, 1115, 44776, 374, 3629, 14183, 311, 439, 330, 4338, 942, 685, 1210, 578, 10334, 315, 25702, 834, 942, 685, 574, 1176, 11223, 555, 54595, 21605, 39750, 5248, 304, 220, 6280, 22, 323, 13533, 430, 1274, 617, 264, 16188, 25835, 311, 8108, 420, 834, 942, 685, 323, 11322, 25702, 29237, 382, 4599, 459, 3927, 374, 41782, 449, 2038, 430, 23093, 31095, 872, 6484, 21463, 477, 33726, 11, 814, 1253, 3217, 25702, 834, 942, 685, 13, 1789, 3187, 11, 422, 4423, 13919, 430, 20149, 374, 53997, 11, 719, 1243, 47310, 430, 20149, 649, 5353, 6129, 2890, 5435, 11, 814, 1253, 2733, 264, 5647, 315, 834, 942, 685, 13, 2057, 8108, 420, 834, 942, 685, 11, 279, 3927, 1253, 2349, 872, 21463, 477, 33726, 311, 5398, 449, 279, 502, 2038, 11, 477, 814, 1253, 25442, 553, 477, 9541, 872, 6484, 21463, 311, 5766, 279, 44776, 382, 34, 51549, 834, 942, 685, 649, 1101, 12446, 994, 459, 3927, 596, 7865, 374, 40240, 449, 872, 33726, 477, 2819, 13, 1789, 2937, 11, 422, 4423, 8349, 311, 907, 48948, 719, 374, 10791, 21078, 11, 814, 1253, 3217, 834, 942, 685, 13, 2057, 8108, 420, 834, 942, 685, 11, 814, 1253, 1456, 311, 9541, 872, 7865, 477, 2349, 872, 33726, 311, 5398, 449, 872, 6299, 382, 28589, 11, 25702, 834, 942, 685, 374, 264, 8147, 24064, 5457, 430, 649, 6678, 7931, 311, 2349, 872, 21463, 11, 33726, 11, 323, 28198, 311, 11322, 264, 5647, 315, 29237, 323, 8108, 279, 44776, 5938, 449, 10168, 52133