Output~2025-04-24 17:42:27.381520: [RequestOutput(request_id=1761, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Explain what rare earth elements are and list some examples. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 83017, 1148, 9024, 9578, 5540, 527, 323, 1160, 1063, 10507, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a response that completes the request:\n\nRare earth elements are a group of 17 elements that are found in the periodic table and are characterized by their unique magnetic, electrical, and chemical properties. They are called "rare" because they are relatively scarce in the Earth\'s crust and are often found in small amounts in minerals. These elements are also known for their high technological applications, making them essential for many modern technologies.\n\nSome examples of rare earth elements include:\n\n1. Neodymium (Nd) - used in permanent magnets, such as those found in electric motors, generators, and wind turbines.\n2. Dysprosium (Dy) - used in magnets, catalysts, and phosphors.\n3. Europium (Eu) - used in phosphors, lasers, and magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) machines.\n4. Terbium (Tb) - used in phosphors, magnets, and catalysts.\n5. Yttrium (Y) - used in superconductors, phosphors, and catalysts.\n6. Lanthanum (La) - used in catalysts, ceramics, and glass.\n7. Cerium (Ce) - used in catalytic converters, glass, and ceramics.\n8. Praseodymium (Pr) - used in magnets, catalysts, and glass.\n9. Samarium (Sm) - used in magnets, catalysts, and nuclear reactors.\n10. Gadolinium (Gd) - used in magnets, catalysts, and medical imaging agents.\n11. Erbium (Er) - used in fiber optic communications, lasers, and phosphors.\n12. Thulium (Tm) - used in lasers, magnets, and nuclear reactors.\n13. Ytterbium (Yb) - used in lasers, magnets, and superconductors.\n14. Lutetium (Lu) - used in catalysts, ceramics, and glass.\n15. Scandium (Sc) - used in aluminum alloys, magnets, and catalysts.\n16. Actinium (Ac) - used in nuclear reactors and medical applications.\n17. Protactinium (Pa) - used in nuclear reactors and medical applications.\n\nThese rare earth elements are essential for many modern technologies, including electronics, renewable energy systems, and medical equipment.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 2077, 430, 45695, 279, 1715, 1473, 67511, 9578, 5540, 527, 264, 1912, 315, 220, 1114, 5540, 430, 527, 1766, 304, 279, 39445, 2007, 323, 527, 32971, 555, 872, 5016, 24924, 11, 20314, 11, 323, 11742, 6012, 13, 2435, 527, 2663, 330, 81, 548, 1, 1606, 814, 527, 12309, 59290, 304, 279, 9420, 596, 40712, 323, 527, 3629, 1766, 304, 2678, 15055, 304, 34072, 13, 4314, 5540, 527, 1101, 3967, 369, 872, 1579, 30116, 8522, 11, 3339, 1124, 7718, 369, 1690, 6617, 14645, 382, 8538, 10507, 315, 9024, 9578, 5540, 2997, 1473, 16, 13, 4275, 1094, 51318, 320, 40937, 8, 482, 1511, 304, 15690, 73780, 11, 1778, 439, 1884, 1766, 304, 9249, 38424, 11, 44163, 11, 323, 10160, 76775, 627, 17, 13, 65142, 782, 82, 2411, 320, 35, 88, 8, 482, 1511, 304, 73780, 11, 51483, 82, 11, 323, 33088, 1105, 627, 18, 13, 68115, 2411, 320, 55218, 8, 482, 1511, 304, 33088, 1105, 11, 72475, 11, 323, 24924, 58081, 32758, 320, 79770, 8, 12933, 627, 19, 13, 10335, 65, 2411, 320, 51, 65, 8, 482, 1511, 304, 33088, 1105, 11, 73780, 11, 323, 51483, 82, 627, 20, 13, 816, 83, 376, 2411, 320, 56, 8, 482, 1511, 304, 2307, 77752, 1105, 11, 33088, 1105, 11, 323, 51483, 82, 627, 21, 13, 445, 32329, 276, 372, 320, 8921, 8, 482, 1511, 304, 51483, 82, 11, 96806, 11, 323, 9168, 6