Output~2025-04-24 17:42:44.060223: [RequestOutput(request_id=1767, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Give me a summary of the process for filing a restraining order. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 21335, 757, 264, 12399, 315, 279, 1920, 369, 26559, 264, 84393, 2015, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is a summary of the process for filing a restraining order:\n\n**Step 1: Determine if a Restraining Order is Necessary**\n\n* Identify the type of restraining order you need: There are several types of restraining orders, including:\n\t+ Temporary Restraining Order (TRO): A temporary order that lasts until a hearing is held to determine if a permanent restraining order should be issued.\n\t+ Permanent Restraining Order (PRO): A long-term order that can last for up to 3 years.\n\t+ Harassment Restraining Order (HRO): A type of restraining order that prohibits someone from harassing or threatening you.\n* Consider the reasons why you need a restraining order: You may need a restraining order if you are experiencing domestic violence, stalking, harassment, or other forms of abuse.\n\n**Step 2: Gather Evidence**\n\n* Collect any evidence that supports your claim, such as:\n\t+ Photos or videos of the abuse or harassment\n\t+ Witness statements\n\t+ Police reports\n\t+ Medical records\n\t+ Text messages, emails, or other written communications\n* Keep all evidence in a safe and secure location, such as a locked box or a secure online storage service.\n\n**Step 3: Fill Out the Petition**\n\n* Obtain a petition for a restraining order from the court or download one from the court's website.\n* Fill out the petition completely and accurately, including:\n\t+ Your name and contact information\n\t+ The name and contact information of the person you are seeking to restrain\n\t+ A detailed description of the abuse or harassment you have experienced\n\t+ The specific relief you are seeking (e.g. a TRO, PRO, or HRO)\n\n**Step 4: File the Petition**\n\n* Take the completed petition to the court and file it with the clerk.\n* Pay the filing fee, which varies by state and court.\n* The clerk will review your petition and determine if it is complete and accurate.\n\n**Step 5: Serve the Respondent**\n\n* The respondent (the person you are seeking to restrain) must be served with a copy of the petition and a summons.\n* You can hire a process server to serve the respondent, or you can ask the court for assistance.\n\n**Step 6: Attend the Hearing**\n\n* A hearing will be scheduled to determine if a restraining order should be issued.\n* At the hearing, you will be required to testify and present your evidence.\n* The respondent will also have the opportunity to testify and present their side of the case", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 12399, 315, 279, 1920, 369, 26559, 264, 84393, 2015, 1473, 334, 8468, 220, 16, 25, 31001, 422, 264, 42427, 2101, 7365, 374, 95633, 57277, 9, 65647, 279, 955, 315, 84393, 2015, 499, 1205, 25, 2684, 527, 3892, 4595, 315, 84393, 10373, 11, 2737, 512, 197, 10, 55548, 42427, 2101, 7365, 320, 51, 1308, 1680, 362, 13643, 2015, 430, 40758, 3156, 264, 11011, 374, 5762, 311, 8417, 422, 264, 15690, 84393, 2015, 1288, 387, 11136, 627, 197, 10, 57316, 42427, 2101, 7365, 320, 9295, 1680, 362, 1317, 9860, 2015, 430, 649, 1566, 369, 709, 311, 220, 18, 1667, 627, 197, 10, 5340, 395, 479, 42427, 2101, 7365, 320, 39, 1308, 1680, 362, 955, 315, 84393, 2015, 430, 59538, 4423, 505, 87270, 477, 27903, 499, 627, 9, 2