with pairs forming during the breeding season and remaining together for several years.\n\n**Habitat and Distribution:**\n\n* The European Goldfinch is found in a variety of habitats, including gardens, parks, and open countryside, as well as woodlands and scrublands.\n* It is a migratory species, with some populations making short-distance migrations, while others remain resident in their year-round territories.\n\n**Conservation Status:**\n\n* The European Goldfinch is listed as a species of "Least Concern" on the International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN) Red List, as it is widely distributed and has a large population.\n* However, the species is declining in some parts of its range due to habitat loss and fragmentation, as well as the introduction of non-native species that compete for food and habitat.\n\nOverall, the European Goldfinch is a striking and charming bird species that is a delight to observe in its natural habitat. Its bright plumage, acrobatic abilities, and social behavior make it a popular bird among birdwatchers and nature enthusiasts.', token_ids=[791, 7665, 7573, 5589, 331, 320, 5889, 4088, 285, 3786, 4088, 285, 8, 374, 264, 2678, 311, 11298, 28935, 12224, 9606, 430, 374, 10068, 311, 4606, 11, 11104, 13936, 11, 323, 4892, 10384, 13, 5810, 527, 1063, 315, 1202, 1401, 17910, 1473, 334, 40353, 85084, 25, 57277, 9, 578, 7665, 7573, 5589, 331, 706, 264, 35947, 14071, 323, 3776, 42272, 425, 11, 449, 264, 10107, 14071, 3663, 11, 28691, 11, 323, 36517, 11, 323, 264, 3776, 2107, 389, 1202, 2010, 627, 9, 1102, 706, 264, 1317, 11, 14618, 9986, 323, 264, 2875, 11, 390, 950, 387, 587, 627, 9, 578, 12224, 11193, 1990, 220, 806, 12, 1032, 10166, 320, 19, 13, 18, 12, 20, 13, 16, 304, 8, 304, 3160, 323, 50542, 2212, 220, 605, 12, 717, 34419, 320, 15, 13, 1758, 12, 15, 13, 3391, 25616, 4390, 9, 11699, 27296, 527, 12309, 2875, 323, 18460, 11, 449, 264, 27296, 857, 315, 2212, 220, 508, 12, 1419, 10166, 320, 22, 13, 24, 12, 24, 13, 16, 304, 3677, 334, 