erage age of all people in the list. Please provide the code and explain your approach.\n\nThis question tests the candidate's ability to work with complex data structures, such as lists and dictionaries, and their understanding of Python's built-in functions and data types.\n\n**Question 4:** Can you write a Python program to scrape the titles of all the articles on a given webpage using the `requests` and `BeautifulSoup` libraries? Please provide the code and explain the steps you took to achieve this.\n\nThis question assesses the candidate's ability to work with web scraping and their understanding of the `requests` and `BeautifulSoup` libraries.\n\n**Question 5:** Suppose you have a large CSV file containing customer data, and you need to filter out customers who have made more than three purchases. Write a Python program to achieve this using the `pandas` library. Please provide the code and explain your approach.\n\nThis question evaluates the candidate's ability to work with large datasets and their understanding of the `pandas` library, as well as their ability to write efficient and readable code.\n\nThese questions are designed to assess the candidate's fluency with Python, their problem-solving skills, and their ability to write clean and efficient code.", token_ids=[8586, 527, 4330, 7274, 4860, 311, 8720, 264, 9322, 596, 20236, 2301, 449, 13325, 1473, 334, 14924, 220, 16, 68063, 3053, 499, 3350, 264, 13325, 2068, 311, 11294, 279, 2694, 315, 682, 1524, 5219, 304, 264, 2728, 1160, 30, 5321, 3493, 279, 2082, 323, 10552, 701, 3463, 1920, 382, 2028, 3488, 8720, 288, 279, 9322, 596, 5845, 311, 3350, 13325, 2082, 323, 872, 8830, 315, 6913, 828, 14726, 323, 2585, 14726, 382, 334, 14924, 220, 17, 68063, 2650, 1053, 499, 4305, 264, 4382, 31052, 304, 13325, 430, 649, 2804, 6913, 35884, 7677, 1093, 5369, 11, 76340, 11, 47544, 11, 323, 13096, 30, 5321, 3493, 264, 2082, 44165, 323, 10552, 279, 12496, 4920, 433, 382, 2028, 3488, 67349, 279, 9322, 596, 5845, 311, 2955,