Output~2025-04-24 17:51:24.548145: [RequestOutput(request_id=1989, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Generate a list of five tips to save money on groceries. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 20400, 264, 1160, 315, 4330, 10631, 311, 3665, 3300, 389, 66508, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here are five tips to help you save money on groceries:\n\n**Tip 1: Plan Your Meals and Make a Grocery List**\n\nBefore you go to the store, plan out your meals for the week and make a list of the ingredients you need. This will help you avoid buying unnecessary items and reduce food waste. You can also use apps like Mealime or Yummly to help you plan your meals and generate a grocery list.\n\n**Tip 2: Shop Sales and Stock Up**\n\nCheck the weekly ads for your local grocery stores and plan your shopping trip around the items that are on sale. Stock up on non-perishable items when they're at their cheapest, and consider buying in bulk if you use a lot of a particular item. Just be sure to check the expiration dates and store the items properly to ensure they stay fresh.\n\n**Tip 3: Shop at Discount Stores and Use Cashback Apps**\n\nConsider shopping at discount stores or dollar stores for non-perishable items like canned goods, pasta, and rice. You can also use cashback apps like Ibotta or Fetch Rewards to earn money back on your grocery purchases. These apps offer rebates on certain items, and you can redeem your rewards for cash or gift cards.\n\n**Tip 4: Buy in Season and Use Unit Prices**\n\nWhen shopping for produce, try to buy items that are in season. They're often cheaper and taste better than out-of-season produce. Also, be sure to check the unit price (price per ounce or pound) to make sure you're getting the best deal. For example, a larger container of yogurt may be cheaper per ounce than a smaller container, even if the price is higher.\n\n**Tip 5: Avoid Processed and Pre-Packaged Foods**\n\nProcessed and pre-packaged foods are often more expensive than whole ingredients. Try to opt for fresh fruits and vegetables, and cook meals from scratch using whole grains and lean proteins. You can also consider buying in bulk and portioning out your own snacks, such as nuts or dried fruit, to save money and avoid added preservatives.\n\nBy following these tips, you can save money on your grocery bill and eat healthy, delicious meals without breaking the bank!", token_ids=[8586, 527, 4330, 10631, 311, 1520, 499, 3665, 3300, 389, 66508, 1473, 334, 16394, 220, 16, 25, 9878, 4718, 96350, 323, 7557, 264, 96681, 1796, 57277, 10438, 499, 733, 311, 279, 3637, 11, 3197, 704, 701, 21644, 369, 279, 2046, 323, 1304, 264, 1160, 315, 279, 14293, 499, 1205, 13, 1115, 690, 1520, 499, 5766, 12096, 26225, 3673, 323, 8108, 3691, 12571, 13, 1472, 649, 1101, 1005, 10721, 1093, 57488, 547, 477, 816, 27054, 398, 311, 1520, 499, 3197, 701, 21644, 323, 7068, 264, 30687, 1160, 382, 334, 16394, 220, 17, 25, 14355, 16207, 323, 12937, 3216, 57277, 4061, 279, 17496, 14058, 369, 701, 2254, 30687, 10756, 323, 3197, 701, 12185, 8577, 2212, 279, 3673, 430, 527, 389, 6412, 13, 12937, 709, 389, 2536, 17453, 819, 481, 3673, 994, 814, 2351, 520, 872, 43149, 11, 323, 2980, 12096, 304, 20155, 422, 499, 1005, 264, 2763, 315, 264, 4040, 1537, 13, 4702, 387, 2771, 311, 1817, 279, 32792, 13003, 323, 3637, 279, 3673, 10489, 311, 6106, 814, 4822, 7878, 382, 334, 16394, 220, 18, 25, 14355, 520, 33759, 39402, 323, 5560, 23139, 1445, 34120, 57277, 38275, 12185, 52