Output~2025-04-24 17:51:33.899315: [RequestOutput(request_id=1991, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Gather key facts about the history of the Death Penalty in the United States. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 50095, 1401, 13363, 922, 279, 3925, 315, 279, 16290, 96342, 304, 279, 3723, 4273, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here are the key facts about the history of the death penalty in the United States:\n\n**Early History (1607-1865)**\n\n* The death penalty was first used in the American colonies in 1608, when Captain George Kendall was executed in Jamestown, Virginia for treason.\n* The first recorded execution in the United States was that of John Billington, a Pilgrim who was hanged in Plymouth Colony in 1630 for murder.\n* The death penalty was used extensively during the colonial period, with various methods of execution including hanging, beheading, and burning at the stake.\n* The first federal execution in the United States was that of Robert Lewis in 1790, who was hanged for murder.\n\n**19th Century (1865-1900)**\n\n* The 18th Amendment to the US Constitution, ratified in 1791, prohibited the federal government from imposing the death penalty for any crime other than treason, piracy, and murder.\n* In the mid-19th century, the death penalty was used to punish crimes such as rape, burglary, and arson.\n* The first electric chair was used in the United States in 1890, when William Kemmler was executed in Auburn, New York.\n* The 14th Amendment to the US Constitution, ratified in 1868, established the principle of due process and limited the use of the death penalty to crimes that were punishable by death at the time of the offense.\n\n**20th Century (1900-2000)**\n\n* The 20th century saw a decline in the use of the death penalty, with many states abolishing it or replacing it with life imprisonment.\n* The first execution by gas chamber was carried out in 1924, when Gee Jon was executed in Nevada for murder.\n* The first execution by lethal injection was carried out in 1982, when Charles Brooks was executed in Texas for murder.\n* The Supreme Court's decision in Furman v. Georgia (1972) led to a moratorium on the death penalty in many states, as the Court ruled that the death penalty was unconstitutional as it was being applied arbitrarily and discriminatorily.\n* The Anti-Terrorism and Effective Death Penalty Act of 1996 and the Prison Litigation Reform Act of 1996 were passed, which made it more difficult for death row inmates to appeal their sentences and for courts to review their cases.\n\n**21st Century (2000-Present)**\n\n* The death penalty remains legal in 28 states in the United States", token_ids=[8586, 527, 279, 1401, 13363, 922, 279, 3925, 315, 279, 4648, 16750, 304, 279, 3723, 4273, 1473, 334, 42298, 11346, 320, 6330, 22, 12, 9714, 20, 33395, 271, 9, 578, 4648, 16750, 574, 1176, 1511, 304, 279, 3778, 49028, 304, 220, 6330, 23, 11, 994, 22022, 10058, 74176, 574, 16070, 304, 93188, 44058, 11, 13286, 369, 79359, 627, 9, 578, 1176, 12715, 11572, 304, 279, 3723, 4273, 574, 430, 315, 3842, 8766, 4910, 11, 264, 37451, 87197, 889, 574, 305, 3811, 304, 72098, 82946, 304, 220, 9892, 15, 369, 10102, 627, 9, 578, 4648, 16750, 574, 1511, 42817, 2391, 279, 37683, 4261, 11, 449, 5370, 5528, 315, 11572, 2737, 21363, 11, 387, 11666, 11, 323, 20252, 520, 279, 18783, 627, 9, 578, 1176, 6918, 11572, 304, 279, 3723, 4273, 574, 430, 315, 8563, 21256, 304, 220, 11128, 15, 11, 889, 574, 305, 3811, 369, 10102, 382, 334, 777, 339, 28200, 320, 9714, 20, 12, 7028, 15, 33395, 271, 9, 578, 220, 972, 339, 22454, 311, 279, 2326, 18039, 11, 97665, 304, 220, 11128, 16, 11, 27010, 279, 6918, 3109, 505, 49941, 279, 4648, 16750, 369, 904, 9977, 1023, 1109, 79359, 11, 78312, 11, 323, 10102, 627, 9, 763, 279, 5209, 12, 777, 339, 9478, 11, 279, 4648, 16750, 574, 1511, 311, 32151, 17073, 1778, 439, 17199, 11, 78043, 11, 323, 87850, 627, 9, 578, 1176, 9249, 10716, 574, 1511, 304, 279, 3723, 4273, 304, 220, 9378, 15, 11, 994, 12656, 67066, 1029, 261, 574, 16070, 304, 53449, 11, 1561, 4356, 627, 9, 578, 220, 975, 339, 22454, 311, 279, 2326, 18039, 11, 97665, 304, 220, 9714, 23, 11, 9749, 279, 17966, 315, 4245, 1920, 323, 7347, 279, 1005, 315, 279, 4648, 16750, 311, 17073, 430, 1051, 81670, 555, 4648, 520, 279, 892, 315, 279, 17193, 382, 334, 508, 339, 28200, 320, 7028, 15, 12, 1049, 15, 33395, 271, 9, 578, 220, 508, 339, 9478, 5602, 264, 18174, 304, 279, 1005, 315, 279, 4648, 16750, 11, 449, 1690, 5415, 37276, 11218, 433, 477, 25935, 433, 449, 2324, 43374, 627, 9, 578, 1176, 11572, 555, 6962, 25199, 574, 11953, 704, 304, 220, 5926, 19, 11, 994, 96697, 12565, 574, 16070, 304, 27966, 369, 10102, 627, 9, 578, 1176, 11572, 555, 45089, 26127, 574, 11953, 704, 304, 220, 3753, 17, 11, 994, 15274, 39119, 574, 16070, 304, 8421, 369, 10102, 627, 9, 578, 13814, 7301, 596, 5597, 304, 50940, 1543, 348, 13, 16272, 320, 4468, 17, 8, 6197, 311, 264, 4411, 66844, 389, 279, 4648, 16750, 304, 1690, 5415, 11, 439, 279, 7301, 21989, 430, 279, 4648, 16750, 574, 53925, 439, 433, 574, 1694, 9435, 86757, 323, 82838, 1570, 627, 9, 578, 23853, 9469, 850, 2191, 323, 48023, 16290, 96342, 3298, 315, 220, 2550, 21, 323, 279, 42618, 39351, 18413, 40365, 3298, 315, 220, 2550, 21, 1051, 5946, 11, 902, 1903, 433, 810, 5107, 369, 4648, 2872, 42712, 311, 14638, 872, 23719, 323, 369, 19359, 311, 3477, 872, 5157, 382, 334, 1691, 267, 28200, 320, 1049, 15, 9483, 2762, 33395, 271, 9, 578, 4648, 16750, 8625, 5897, 304,