Output~2025-04-24 17:53:04.423478: [RequestOutput(request_id=2012, prompt='<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{\'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Describe the content of the novel "The Great Gatsby". ### Response:\'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n', prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 61885, 279, 2262, 315, 279, 11775, 330, 791, 8681, 480, 36614, 3343, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="The Great Gatsby, written by F. Scott Fitzgerald, is a classic novel set in the 1920s in Long Island, New York. The story revolves around the mysterious millionaire Jay Gatsby and his obsession with winning back his lost love, Daisy Buchanan.\n\nThe novel is narrated by Nick Carraway, a young man from the Midwest who moves to Long Island's West Egg to work in the bond business. Nick rents a small house next to Gatsby's grand mansion, where he becomes fascinated by his neighbor's lavish lifestyle and enigmatic character.\n\nAs the story unfolds, it becomes clear that Gatsby and Daisy had a romantic relationship before she married the wealthy and brutish Tom Buchanan. Gatsby is determined to win her back, and he uses his wealth and influence to try to make that happen. Through various means, including throwing extravagant parties and buying a luxurious car, Gatsby attempts to impress Daisy and win her heart.\n\nMeanwhile, Tom is having an affair with Myrtle Wilson, a working-class woman who is trapped in a loveless marriage. When Gatsby and Daisy's affair is discovered, it sets off a chain of tragic events that ultimately leads to the death of Myrtle's husband, George, and the destruction of Gatsby's American Dream.\n\nThroughout the novel, Fitzgerald explores themes of class, wealth, love, and the corrupting influence of materialism. The characters are complex and multi-dimensional, with Gatsby being a symbol of the elusive and unattainable American Dream. The novel is known for its vivid descriptions of the Jazz Age, its critique of the excesses of the wealthy, and its poignant portrayal of the fragility of human relationships.\n\nUltimately, The Great Gatsby is a haunting and thought-provoking novel that explores the darker side of the American Dream and the consequences of chasing after something that may be unattainable.", token_ids=[791, 8681, 480, 36614, 11, 5439, 555, 435, 13, 10016, 62314, 11, 374, 264, 11670, 11775, 743, 304, 279, 220, 5926, 15, 82, 304, 5843, 10951, 11, 1561, 4356, 13, 578, 3446, 79476, 2212, 279, 26454, 90044, 19455, 480, 36614, 323, 813, 49635, 449, 11230, 1203, 813, 5675, 3021, 11, 71264, 85290, 382, 791, 11775, 374, 13713, 660, 555, 15341, 3341, 1059, 352, 11, 264, 3995, 893, 505, 279, 52257, 889, 11031, 311, 5843, 10951, 596, 4410, 42313, 311, 990, 304, 279, 11049, 2626, 13, 15341, 63090, 264, 2678, 3838, 1828, 311, 480, 36614, 596, 6800, 52528, 11, 1405, 568, 9221, 61914, 555, 813, 9760, 596, 80234, 19433, 323, 665, 99830, 3752, 382, 2170, 279, 3446, 90765, 11, 433, 9221, 2867, 430, 480, 36614, 323, 71264, 1047, 264, 24364, 5133, 1603, 1364, 12502, 279, 28994, 323, 19968, 819, 8529, 85290, 13, 480, 36614, 374, 11075, 311, 3243, 1077, 1203, 11, 323, 568, 5829, 813, 12205, 323, 10383, 311, 1456, 311, 1304, 430, 3621, 13, 17331, 5370, 3445, 11, 2737, 21939, 95950, 9875, 323, 12096, 264, 43828, 1841, 11, 480, 36614, 13865, 311, 10098, 71264, 323, 3243, 1077, 4851, 382, 26054, 11, 8529, 374, 3515, 459, 31017, 449, 3092, 93536, 17882, 11, 264, 3318, 15144, 5333, 889, 374, 31691, 304, 264, 3021, 1752, 11103, 13, 3277, 480, 36614, 323, 71264, 596, 31017, 374, 11352, 11, 433, 7437, 1022, 264, 8957, 315, 35279, 4455, 430, 13967, 11767, 311, 279, 4648, 315, 3092, 93536, 596, 10177, 11, 10058, 11, 323, 279, 19814, 315, 480, 36614, 596, 3778, 18308, 382, 60105, 279, 11775, 11, 62314, 41424, 22100, 315, 538, 11, 12205, 11, 3021, 11, 323, 279, 22681, 287, 10383, 315, 3769, 2191, 13, 578, 5885, 527, 6485, 323, 7447, 33520, 11, 449, 480, 36614, 1694, 264, 7891, 315, 279, 66684, 323, 653, 1617, 467, 481, 3778, 18308, 13, 578, 11775, 374, 3967, 369, 1202, 43120, 28887, 315, 279, 36967, 13381, 11, 1202, 43665, 315, 279, 13937, 288, 315, 279, 28994, 11, 323, 1202, 93447, 75033, 315, 279, 8508, 1429, 315, 3823, 12135, 382, 67343, 11, 578, 8681, 480, 36614, 374, 264, 77754, 323, 3463, 10039, 85, 10979, 11775, 430, 41424, 279, 40130, 3185, 315, 279, 3778, 18308, 323, 279, 16296, 315, 43931, 1306, 2555, 430, 1253, 387, 653, 1617, 467, 481, 13, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None)], finished=True, metrics=None, lora_request=None, num_cached_tokens=None, multi_modal_placeholders={})]
