Output~2025-04-24 17:55:36.240736: [RequestOutput(request_id=2068, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write a news article that discusses two recent events ### Input: IBM announcement of new Quantum Computing initiative | new YouTube Music feature ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 264, 3754, 4652, 430, 35434, 1403, 3293, 4455, 17010, 5688, 25, 29022, 17480, 315, 502, 56413, 46879, 20770, 765, 502, 13674, 10948, 4668, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='**HEADLINE:** IBM Takes Leap into Quantum Computing, YouTube Music Revolutionizes Music Discovery\n\nIn a double dose of innovation, two major tech giants have made significant announcements that are set to shape the future of their respective industries. IBM has unveiled a new Quantum Computing initiative, while YouTube has launched a groundbreaking new feature for music lovers.\n\n**IBM\'s Quantum Computing Initiative**\n\nIBM has taken a major step forward in the field of quantum computing with the announcement of its new initiative, aimed at harnessing the power of quantum computing to solve some of the world\'s most complex problems. The company has been at the forefront of quantum computing research for several years, and this new initiative marks a significant milestone in its journey to bring this technology to the mainstream.\n\nThe initiative will focus on developing practical applications for quantum computing in areas such as medicine, finance, and climate modeling. IBM\'s quantum computers will be used to simulate complex systems, optimize processes, and analyze vast amounts of data, leading to breakthroughs in fields such as cancer research, financial modeling, and weather forecasting.\n\n"We are excited to take the next step in our journey to make quantum computing a reality," said IBM\'s CEO, Arvind Krishna. "Our goal is to make quantum computing accessible to businesses and researchers, and to help them unlock its potential to solve some of the world\'s most pressing challenges."\n\n**YouTube Music\'s New Feature**\n\nMeanwhile, YouTube has launched a new feature that is set to revolutionize the way we discover and enjoy music. The new feature, called "Reels," allows users to create and share short, engaging videos that showcase their favorite songs and artists.\n\nReels can be up to 60 seconds long and can include a combination of music, lyrics, and visuals. Users can add filters, effects, and captions to make their Reels more engaging, and can share them with friends, family, or the wider YouTube community.\n\nThe feature is designed to make music discovery more social and interactive, allowing users to connect with other music lovers and discover new artists and genres. YouTube has also partnered with major music labels and artists to provide exclusive content and promotions.\n\n"We are thrilled to introduce Reels, a new way for our users to express themselves and connect with others through music," said YouTube\'s CEO, Susan Wojcicki. "We believe that music has the power to bring people together, and we are excited to see how our users will use Reels to share their passion for music with the world."\n\n**Conclusion**\n\nThese two announcements mark significant milestones in the development of quantum', token_ids=[334, 36533, 8429, 68063, 29022, 38707, 72382, 1139, 56413, 46879, 11, 13674, 10948, 22910, 4861, 10948, 39193, 271, 644, 264