Output~2025-04-24 17:55:42.185028: [RequestOutput(request_id=2069, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Output me a product design guide that is easy to understand ### Input: Design guide for tech product involving AI & robotics with a cartoon theme ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9442, 757, 264, 2027, 2955, 8641, 430, 374, 4228, 311, 3619, 17010, 5688, 25, 7127, 8641, 369, 13312, 2027, 16239, 15592, 612, 74706, 449, 264, 31449, 7057, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="**Product Design Guide: WhizBot - A Cartoon-Themed AI & Robotics Companion**\n\n**Overview**\n\nWhizBot is a cutting-edge AI-powered robot designed to assist and entertain children aged 6-12. With its cartoon-inspired design, WhizBot aims to make learning and exploration fun and engaging. This product design guide outlines the key features, functionality, and design principles that will bring WhizBot to life.\n\n**Design Principles**\n\n1. **Fun and Playful**: WhizBot's design should be approachable, colorful, and engaging, making it appealing to children.\n2. **Easy to Use**: The interface should be intuitive, allowing children to easily interact with WhizBot and access its features.\n3. **Educational**: WhizBot's AI capabilities should provide a fun and interactive learning experience, teaching children about AI, robotics, and STEM concepts.\n4. **Safety First**: WhizBot's design should prioritize safety, ensuring it is safe for children to use and interact with.\n\n**Design Elements**\n\n1. **Body**: WhizBot's body will be a rounded, anthropomorphic shape with a bright, cartoon-inspired color scheme. The body will be made of a durable, child-friendly material.\n2. **Face**: WhizBot's face will feature a large, expressive screen that displays emotions and animations, making it more relatable and engaging for children.\n3. **Arms and Legs**: WhizBot will have two arms and two legs, allowing it to move around and interact with its environment.\n4. **Screen**: The screen will display a variety of interactive elements, including games, educational content, and animations.\n5. **Microphone and Speaker**: WhizBot will be equipped with a high-quality microphone and speaker, enabling it to communicate with children and respond to their voice commands.\n\n**Features**\n\n1. **AI-Powered Learning**: WhizBot will use AI to adapt to a child's learning style and pace, providing personalized educational content and feedback.\n2. **Robotics**: WhizBot will be able to move around and interact with its environment, allowing children to explore and learn about robotics and programming.\n3. **Games and Activities**: WhizBot will offer a range of games and activities that teach STEM concepts, such as coding, problem-solving, and critical thinking.\n4. **Voice Assistant**: WhizBot will be able to respond to voice commands, allowing children to control its movements and interactions.\n\n**Design Considerations**\n\n1. **Safety**: WhizBot's", token_ids=[334, 4921, 7127, 13002, 25, 1254, 450, 24406, 482, 362, 69530, 71626, 16809, 15592, 612, 77564, 70075, 57277, 334, 42144, 57277, 1671, 450, 24406, 374, 264, 14713, 48448, 15592, 41503, 12585, 6319, 311, 7945, 323, 46276, 2911, 20330, 220, 21, 12, 717, 13, 3161, 1202, 31449, 53161, 2955, 11, 1254, 450, 24406, 22262, 311, 1304, 6975, 323, 27501, 2523, 323, 23387, 13, 1115, 2027, 2955, 8641, 50729, 279, 1401, 4519, 11,